MANILA (Reuters) - The Philippine Volcanology Agency on Thursday raised the alert level of a volcanic eruption near the capital Manila after the volcano spewed ash and smoke into the air at a height of 1 km. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, July 1, 2021.
The Philippine Volcanology Agency has raised the alert level from No. 2 to No. 3 for Taal Volcano, 70 km south of Manila. At the same time, the Philippine authorities also ordered the evacuation of people near the Taal volcano to safety.
