The Ministry of Economy and Finance is reviewing and evaluating the "Draft Law on Social Protection System"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Economy and Finance on July 1, 2021 organized a workshop to review and evaluate the "Draft Law on Social Protection System" through a video system chaired by Mr. Ros Silva, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance. Finance and Chairman of the Executive Committee of the National Council for Social Protection.
The draft law on the social protection system has 10 chapters and 91 articles, aiming to ensure the well-being and reduce economic and financial vulnerabilities, strengthen the security of people's income, and promote social equality through the establishment and management of the social protection system. An environment of progress and sustainability.
Mr. Ros Silva stated that with the vision of transforming Cambodia from a low-middle-income country to a high-middle-income country by 2030 and a high-income country by 2050, the Royal Government strongly recognizes The role of social protection system development.
He added that in the spirit of ensuring the income security of the people, the Royal Government has set a long-term vision for the development of the social protection system, which is to build a social protection system that is environmentally efficient and financially sustainable as a tool to reduce and Prevent poverty, vulnerability and inequality.
He stressed that the National Social Protection Policy Framework 2016-2025 has played an important role in increasing access to services, coverage of the National Social Assistance Program and the social security system for public and private sector officials and the people of the economic sector. Out of the citizen system.
He said that at the same time, the Royal Government of Cambodia has the National Social Protection Council as a staff to coordinate and orient policy and a joint strategy on social protection policy development with all relevant ministries and institutions. Achieve many notable big and new achievements, such as:
* Implementation of the Social Security, Occupational Risk and Health Care Regulations for persons subject to the provisions of the Labor Law, including persons working on air and sea vessels and domestic servants, and preparing to submit Implement the social security system for pensions for individuals subject to the provisions of the Labor Law in the near future (mid-2022).
* Implementation of the Social Security Regime on Occupational Risks for Individuals in the Public Sector.
* Implementation of the social security system for health care for individuals in the public sector, former civil servants and veterans.
* Implementation of health care system through health equity fund system for informal workers. * Additional allowances for female workers during childbirth. * Implementation of cash subsidies for pregnant women and children under 2 years of age. * Implementation of school feeding programs using community-based agricultural products. * Launch of the "Kantha Bopha Foundation of Cambodia".
