But in the face of growing Chinese influence and military activity, including North Korea's continued development of missiles and nuclear weapons programs, is Japan still adamant that it does not want nuclear weapons? Will the United States agree to allow Japan to have nuclear weapons?
* Nuclear umbrella
To urge friendly or allied countries not to produce or acquire nuclear weapons, the United States has promised to protect them with its nuclear weapons, commonly known as "nuclear umbrellas." Countries under the US nuclear umbrella include NATO member states, Japan, South Korea and Australia.
On the other hand, allowing Japan to acquire nuclear weapons could encourage other US allies, such as South Korea, Australia or Saudi Arabia, to acquire nuclear weapons, and if new nuclear powers emerge. Next, what does it mean to be an American superpower? America's salty saliva may also be fading.
In 2014, Japan was reported to have 9 tons of plutonium and another 35 tons in France and the United Kingdom, and Japan also had 1.2 tons of uranium. These substances are enough for Japan to produce more than 5,000 nuclear bombs, and it is believed that if Japan really wants to build nuclear weapons, it will not be difficult for Japan, as both Japanese scientists, technology and resources have Not lacking.
But the biggest obstacle to Japan's nuclear weapons is the opposition from the Japanese people. The principle of non-proliferation is Japan's national identity and is deeply involved in domestic politics. According to opinion polls, the vast majority of Japanese people do not support Japan's use of nuclear weapons, despite threats from North Korea or increased Chinese military activity in the region.
The Japanese are seen as content under the protection of the United States nuclear umbrella. Of course, ordinary umbrellas do not completely block the sun or rain. The United States 'nuclear umbrella, too, could not completely dispel the Allies' fears. In this sense, the Japanese leadership is not 100 percent sure that the United States can defend Japan at any time.
Japan currently has territorial disputes with Russia over the Kuril Islands, with China in the East China Sea, as well as past disputes with North Korea, which could put Japan at risk of war at any time. . According to international security experts such as Anders Corr, Japan needs to have nuclear weapons because it is surrounded by Russia, China and North Korea, all of which have nuclear weapons in their hands.
