Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the opportunity for private companies to use quick test equipment to test the health of employees (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, July 1, 2021, announced the opportunity Private companies can use rapid test equipment to test the health of their employees or workers to easily manage and send them to the hospital quickly if positive Kovid 19 is found.
During a video conference to discuss and address the spread of Kovid 19 in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen affirmed that while providing opportunities for private companies to use the rapid test kit, the Ministry The health department has to send a team of doctors to teach private companies how to use the device.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "I would like to call on all private companies to manage their workers when there is a test on their own staff." In order to manage quickly, it is necessary to enable this test, which each company tests itself, and this test training does not take as long as two hours.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia stressed that in the event that a private company can test its staff or workers, the state does not lose anything. On the contrary, it is only profitable because they volunteer to test themselves and in case of illness they go to the doctor for treatment, so the prince decided to give the right to a private company to do this work on his staff.
At this point, Samdech Techo Prime Minister emphasized that this test work should not wait for doctors to teach people how to protect themselves, and if they wait for doctors, they will not be able to perform their work in a timely manner because of the large number of doctors. Less than you need to come to the test, so there may be delays or premature management of the situation.
Apart from private companies, Samdech Techo Hun Sen has ordered the military, police and police units to conduct a quick test on the forces to be able to find them immediately. Therefore, when the ordered rapid test equipment arrives, it must be divided into parts for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to be distributed to subordinate units.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia to fight against Kovid 19 is to find and control people quickly so that they do not spread in the open. The prince said that this point had just been said but had not yet been put into practice, so from now on it must be put into practice.
Please be informed that according to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Royal Government of Cambodia has already ordered this quick test kit from South Korea and will be ready to ship about 1 million in the near future.
Regarding the use of this rapid test equipment, Samdech Techo also instructed the Ministry of Health to supply to other provinces to manage and timely. And in the capitals and provinces, in case of need, also need to immediately request additional to use in full, because the Royal Government does not lack the budget to purchase this equipment.
(Phnom Penh): In the five months from January to May 2021, the trade volume between Cambodia and China reached a total of nearly 4 billion US dollars, an increase of nearly 25% compared to the same period in 2020. . This is according to the report of the Ministry of Commerce.
Speaking to Fresh News, Pen Sovicheat, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Commerce, said that from January to May 2021, the volume of bilateral free trade between Cambodia and China has improved.
Mr. Pen Sovichet added that Cambodian goods exported to the Chinese market include: rice, dried potatoes, fresh mangoes and cashew nuts and many other goods, while goods imported from China include electronics, processed foods. Etc. etc.
Cambodia and China concluded negotiations on a free trade agreement and signed it on October 12, 2020 between the leaders of the two countries. This agreement will enter into force after both parties complete the internal procedures.
Many Cambodian agricultural products will be imported into the Chinese market duty-free through this agreement. The agreement is expected to increase the presence of Cambodian products in the Chinese market and also help attract investors to Cambodia.
China is the largest source of foreign direct investment as well as tourists to Cambodia and also Cambodia's most important trading partner. Donors Donate Some Points and Funds to Poipet City Administration for Use in Kovid Campaign
