The Ministry of Public Works used a mobile scale to weigh sand trucks on the streets in Takhmao City, found 11 overweight vehicles, fined and detained for one year
(Kandal): The Steering Committee for Inspection of Overweight Vehicles of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, on July 1, 2021, in cooperation with officials of Kandal Provincial Scale Station, stopped vehicles to inspect and weigh mobile scales in Takhmao City. Eleven offending vehicles were found, fined and detained for one year, but only one was fined.
The operation was led by Mr. Seng Chhuon, Secretary of State and Chairman of the Standing Committee for Overweight Trucks, and Mr. Kimsan, Undersecretary of State and Deputy Chairman, with the participation of Mr. Chuor Chhun Leng, Representative of the Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport. Kandal Province.
According to the report, during the operation to stop and check the mobile scales, the police found 10 sand trucks that were overweight and sent to be stored on a plot of land in Takhmao City to comply with the law. One unit is only a fine.
However, experts confirmed that for the 10 vehicles carrying more than 20 percent sand will be stored for one year as a penalty.
According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, the team will proceed with the procedure without understanding anyone if it is found that the trucks dare to carry overweight. The operation will continue throughout Kandal province and across the country to restrict transportation in accordance with the law to prevent criminals from arbitrarily destroying roads.
It should be informed that the activities of seizing the offending vehicle were carried out in 3 locations in Kandal province, first: in Kandal Stung district, with fines and detention for 8 offending vehicles, second: in Khsach Kandal district, fined and detained for one year for 8 offending vehicles;
