Thai soldiers arrest 14 Cambodian workers in illegal border crossing
(Banteay Meanchey): 14 different groups of Cambodian workers who smuggled into Thailand illegally were arrested by Thai soldiers at 10:19 pm on June 29, 2021, while the brokers escaped. .
According to the Thai Border Patrol, the 12th Border Patrol Police and the Bopha Forces arrested five Cambodian workers, including three males and two females, in the area of Tap Siem village, Tapraya commune. Ta Praya district, Sa Kaeo province, after the arrest, the police took him to Banteay for interrogation.
When questioned, the workers said that they all went to Thailand to find work and then left Banteay Meanchey province with a Cambodian broker to guide them through the corridor to Thailand at a cost. Brokers 7,000 baht per person.
After interrogation, Thai authorities took all Cambodian workers to make arrest records and follow the rules of health and sent them back to Cambodia through O Bei Choan checkpoint in O'Chrov district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Later, they arrived in Cambodia and the 14 workers were sent to Chattalysak in Thmar Puok district for 14 days before returning home.
