Ministry of Interior warns Cambodian Reform Party for political activities without official registration
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Interior of Cambodia on June 30, 2021 issued a letter warning the Cambodian Reform Party, a party formed by former leaders of the Cambodia National Rescue Party (CNRP) to engage in political activities. Official registration yet.
According to a letter from Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, to Mr. Tin Sai, the founding representative of the Cambodian Reform Party, which was received by Fresh News, the Ministry of Interior has confirmed that the Cambodian Reform Party has not yet registered. Political parties at the Ministry of Interior yet.
The Ministry of Interior added that in the past, the Ministry has observed that the party is conducting political activities in Phnom Penh and in some provinces, these activities are in violation of the provisions of Article 9 and Article 19 new. Of the Law on Political Parties.
The Ministry of Interior also warned the Cambodian Reform Party to stop all political activities at the grassroots level until it was registered as a political party at the Ministry of Interior in accordance with the spirit of the letter of the Ministry of Interior as stated in the reference. On.
The "Cambodian Reform Party" was formed by Ou Chanrath, a former CNRP lawmaker, and his party to run in the 2022 and 2023 national elections after losing faith in the former CNRP leader.
