(Phnom Penh): In order for each election to be free, fair and just to increase the trust of the electorate, all election officials must respect and implement the election law, regulations and ethical procedures in force. This was emphasized by Mr. Prach Chan, Chairman of the National Election Committee (NEC) at the inauguration ceremony held at the NEC office on June 30, 2021.
He said that since 1998 until now, Cambodia has held 16 self-elections. All elections, both universal and non-universal, were held regularly in accordance with the rule of law and were evaluated by the national and international community as smooth, secure, safe, free, fair and just in both legal and technical aspects.
For the next phase from 2021 to 2024, according to the election law, the NEC will hold four elections:
* Commune / Sangkat Council Election 5th Mandate 2022 * 7th National Assembly Election 2023 * 5th Mandate Senate Election 2024 * Capital, Provincial Council and Municipal Council Elections District Council, Khan Council, 4th mandate, 2024.
At the same time, the NEC has been organizing the first election to elect the newly formed Bokor City Council of Kampot Province, which is scheduled to take place on July 25, 2021. The NEC also plans to review the 2021 voter list and voter registration from October 2021.
Taking this opportunity, the new NEC Chairman called on all stakeholders, both national and international, to continue to cooperate with the NEC in accordance with their roles and responsibilities in accordance with the provisions of laws, regulations and laws. The methods, including the legal documents that have been put into force, contribute to the better implementation of the principles of multi-party liberal democracy in Cambodia.
