In 100 years, the Chinese Communist Party has grown from 50 members to 95 million and is the largest ruling party in the world.
The Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) has announced that over the past 100 years, the Communist Party of China (CPC) has transformed from a weak party into one of the largest and most powerful parties in the world, and its membership has grown significantly. Quite a lot, too. The Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) has announced that the number of party members will increase from just 50 to more than 95 million as of June 5, 2021.
On the occasion of the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China noted that its membership has grown steadily, with the number of young members continuing to grow. The number of members and members of ethnic minorities has been steadily increasing. Workers and farmers remain an important part of the party.
On the occasion of the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of China, more and more leading figures from all walks of life have applied to join the party.
The Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) stressed that the results show that the CPC is vibrant and that the cause of the CPC is full of progress.
Wang Wentian, Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, said in his remarks that after a century of hardships, the Communist Party of China has developed into the world's largest ruling party. .
China is now the world's second-largest economy, with an average per capita GDP of more than 10,000 US dollars and eradicating poverty, the ambassador said. Completely contributes more than 30% to global economic growth throughout the year.
Faced with unprecedented Kovid-19 virus, China has achieved remarkable results in preventing the disease, with more than 1 billion doses of Kovid vaccination and the number of Kovid vaccines delivered. Overseas, more than 300 million doses. By 2020, China will have exported more than 224.2 billion masks, 2.31 billion pieces of protective clothing and 27.1 million respirators.
