In Cambodia, deer are present in almost all protected areas, they are also present in the grasslands of Indochina and Borneo. According to data obtained by the Ministry of Environment, the deer has recently been present in various protected areas in Cambodia.
According to Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, deer are relatively endangered and endangered by hunting or trapping dogs. Be food and dangerous because wild animals eat meat.
Normally, this animal makes rapid jumps and jumps in an emergency, but after a short run, it often stops and checks the situation around itself. In communication, the little deer often taps its hind legs on the ground or sticks quickly as a marker. This animal has a high ability to reproduce after 150-170 days of gestation, sometimes giving birth to twins, but rarely.
Regarding wildlife conservation, Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that although deer are a relatively endangered species in protected areas, it is necessary to increase the attention, protection and conservation like other species. Wildlife is an invaluable natural resource for Cambodia and extremely valuable for biodiversity and ecosystems.
The Ministry of Environment has developed various strategic plans for the protection and conservation of wildlife in Cambodia, focusing on the protection of forests, habitats, food sources and water sources, because these factors are very important for the survival of wildlife.
