(Kampong Speu): Sadly, a rare adult female squirrel died after being trapped by a wild hunter, while experts from the Wildlife Alliance went to the rescue, but due to the very serious condition that is close. He died of asphyxiation and was unable to stand and lost part of his front leg due to the trap.
Veterinarians administered sedatives to the animals before applying antibiotics. But unfortunately, because it was too weak, he died under anesthesia. A squirrel was injured in the back of a field in the Oral Mountains Wildlife Sanctuary on June 18, 2021. This is according to the report of the Wildlife Alliance received on June 30, 2021.
"Their chances of survival are low, and most of the trapped animals die from their injuries," said Nick Mark, director of wildlife rescue and care at the Wildlife Alliance. " By the time the trapped animals are found, most are dead. “They die very slowly and painfully. "The loss of this stork is bad news for the species, which is globally classified as a vulnerable species."
The Wildlife Alliance is shocked that traps of many animals in Cambodia, including endangered species such as elephants. Baby elephants are often trapped and die, and at least 50 percent of baby elephants are found with severe snare wounds on their legs and trunks through automated cameras.
Last year, wildlife rescue and rescue teams rescued three trapped wild cattle in Kampong Speu and Oddar Meanchey provinces, but unfortunately they all died before arriving. Therefore, to combat the threat to wildlife, conservation NGOs are working with the Ministry of Environment to patrol the forest and remove traps.
For example, the Wildlife Alliance supports the Cardamom Mountain Wildlife Sanctuary, which protected the Cardamom Rainforest last year. The park rangers in the seven Cardamom Mountain Protected Areas have removed 25,886 traps.
