The Royal Government of Cambodia continues to provide allowances to garment and tourism workers and tax incentives for a further three months.
According to the press release, in the spirit of unremitting efforts and high responsibility, the Royal Government has decided to take a series of necessary measures in order to control the spread of Kovid-19 and continue to promote business balance in Areas severely affected.
After factories, enterprises and businesses in the garment, textile, footwear, travel products, bags and tourism sectors receive a permit to suspend employment contract and / or a permit to suspend employment contract from the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training. In accordance with the criteria and conditions for the suspension of the employment contract, the Royal Government of Cambodia will:
* The Royal Government continues to provide a stipend of US $ 40 per month for one worker working in the garment, textile, footwear, travel products and bags sector for an additional three months from July to September 2021.
* Continue to provide a stipend of US $ 40 per month to one worker working in the tourism sector, such as hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies for an additional three months from July to September 2021.
* Enterprises and businesses in the tourism sector must contribute on a voluntary and practical basis in addition to what the Royal Government has to offer.
* Continue to exempt all types of monthly taxes for hotels, guesthouses, restaurants and travel agencies registered with the General Department of Taxation and have business activities in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Kep, Kampot Bavet and Poipet for an additional three months from July to September 2021.
These businesses are still required to file a tax return and use the online value-added tax (E-VAT) system on a monthly basis during the exemption period.
* Continue to waive the payment of social security contributions for occupational risk and health care of the National Social Security Fund during the suspension or suspension of business operations.
* Continue to postpone the implementation of the social security pension system for another 6 months, until the end of December 2021.
The delay will be based on a continuous assessment of the actual socio-economic situation. A fire broke out at a gas station in Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province, killing one person due to electric shock while spraying fuel
(Kampong Cham): A fire broke out at Depotela gas station in Popreng village, Speu commune, Chamkar Leu district, Kampong Cham province on the night of June 29, 2021, killing one person and destroying a lot of property at the scene. . While the cause is due to electric shock (fuel injection can cause an explosion).
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, confirmed that after receiving the information, he immediately ordered the inspection force led by the district police inspector, provincial force, border police inspectorate force to immediately intervene with fire trucks.
