U.S. military spokesman Lt. Col. Wayne Marotto did not provide details about the rocket attack, saying only that no U.S. troops were injured in the attack. The devastation is still under evaluation.
The U.S. military on Sunday reportedly carried out airstrikes on two Iranian-backed militant weapons depots in Syria and one in Iraq. The Syrian Observatory for Human Rights claims that the attack also killed at least five militants.
The airstrikes were carried out under the direct command of Joe Biden, and it is the second time he has ordered such attacks on pro-Iranian militants since taking office. In January.
