(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Customs Administration was formally established during the French colonial period by Royal Kram No. 661 NS dated June 29, 1951.
Subsequently, the Cambodian Customs Administration was renamed the management structure and location as the political trends, chronic civil war, and social and economic context changed from one period to another, leading to the establishment of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia. Currently under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
As of 2021, the Cambodian Customs and Excise Administration, which is the institution in charge of managing, controlling and collecting all kinds of taxes and fees on export and import goods, is 70 years old. June 29, 2021 is the historic day of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia in organizing the celebration of the 70th anniversary of the establishment of the Cambodian Customs Administration.
With this 70th anniversary, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also sent a message to the leaders and civil servants of the Cambodian Customs and Excise to celebrate the birthday of the institution playing an important role in earning this national income.
In this congratulatory message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen highlighted some of the background of the establishment and development process of this institution. The Prime Minister of Cambodia also praised the leadership of civil servants of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as the General Department of Customs and Excise for their attention and efforts to achieve good results in raising funds for the nation. On the collection of import and export taxes.
In this message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded the leaders of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as the General Department of Customs and Excise to continue to pay more attention to achieve better results on management and Collect customs duties.
Due to the fact that Cambodia is currently facing the crisis of the 19 epidemic of Kovid, through this message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also did not forget to remind the leadership of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, as well as the General Department of Customs and Excise. Take care to prevent and participate in the fight against the spread of Kovid 19 by strictly following the rules of the Ministry of Health.
