The Prey Veng provincial administration has appealed to those who have had direct or indirect contact with the above-mentioned Kovid-19 positive individuals to be isolated, monitored for 14 days, and reported to the authorities for sampling and biopsy. Six priority areas identified in Mondulkiri Tourism Development Master Plan
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government has identified six key priority areas for tourism development in Mondulkiri province. This is according to the press release on the result of the meeting of the National Committee for Tourism Development to discuss the report summarizing the results of the master plan for tourism development in Mondulkiri province (2021-2035) at Fresh News on June 29. This 2021.
The six main priority areas are:
First, the ecotourism and ecotourism corridors of the five wildlife sanctuaries (Phnom Prech Nam, Lear, Lumphat, Keo Seima and Sre Pok wildlife sanctuaries), which allow only investment and development of environmentally conscious tourism activities.
Second, the Busra-Dak Dam Cultural Tourism and Ecotourism Corridor, which encourages the development of only ecotourism and ecotourism activities linked to indigenous cultural tourism.
Third: Sen Monorom city, which is a collection of multi-purpose tourism activities.
Fourthly, Oreang district area is connected with the Mondulkiri airport development project, which can be developed as a satellite town area connected with Sen Monorom city.
Fifth, the urban area of Koh Nhek district, which has the potential to be developed as a tourist center in the future, and the development is more extensive than in the conservation area of the wildlife sanctuary.
Sixth: Integrated tourist areas along the border, which allow the development of integrated resorts.
The Master Plan for Tourism Development in Mondulkiri Province (2021-2035) identifies the following key visions:
* Mondulkiri must be identified as an international eco-tourism destination and an important province in the supply of flowers, vegetables and fruits to meet domestic demand and reach exports to foreign markets.
* Contribute to the northeastern region with Mondulkiri as the fourth economic pole after Phnom Penh, coastal areas and Siem Reap and integrate Mondulkiri with other parts of the country and region.
* Maintain a strong balance between economic development, tourism and cross-sectoral support with the conservation of natural resources, indigenous cultural heritage, ensure the maximum fruits of socio-economic development based on the principle of equitable distribution of benefits to Stakeholders.
The Master Plan is an integration plan with a number of key inter-sectoral support areas to serve as a key compass pointing out key mechanisms and strategic directions to meet the five-year national development vision (2021-2035) and the coming years. Based on the current situation and the clear commitment of the Royal Government, focusing on three main objectives:
First, Mondulkiri is a high quality tourist destination.
Second, Mondulkiri is a smart and innovative economic center and a center for the Northeast.
Third, Mondulkiri is a province that has a clear idea of the concept of "conservation for development and development supports conservation."
