General knowledge: A terrifying thing that the Mongol army always does when there is a shortage of food.
(Phnom Penh): Water flowing from the hills always moves fast, interfering with the surrounding lowlands, and so does the expansion of the Mongol Empire, due to the skillful leadership of kings and commanders, and their armies. Outstanding strength, too.
The secret of the Mongol army is a terrifying thing that they do every time they are in a long battle or travel until they run out of food. If they are too hungry, they often operate on the horse's blood vessels in the neck and suck enough blood to survive, and then close the horse's wounds.
Another special feature of the Mongol army was that even in the face of death, they were not afraid to attack the enemy. They are a very disciplined and very patient army. The Mongol army was able to travel for 2-3 days without having to stop eating.
Mongol soldiers were able to shoot a bow from a horse's back at a distance of 200-400 meters and hit a moving target. Not only that, they are also famous for training hawks and eagles to be used to carry messages or shout, signal or announce something skillfully. Court Detains Fake National Police and Fake Documents of General Commission of National Police and Ministry of Interior
