Army teams have become a major force in helping to vaccinate people. After the successful vaccination operation for the people in the red area in Phnom Penh, the vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense has been given new tasks to vaccinate the people in the provinces.
The provinces where the army received orders from the Royal Government for the first vaccination operation were Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampong Speu and Takeo provinces, which launched on June 22. In these four provinces, the army has to cover 810,000 people.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Operation Kovid 19 Vaccination, the Ministry of National Defense regularly monitors the vaccination process and inspects each vaccination destination.
General Ith Sarath noted that the vaccination process went well. In particular, the army as a vaccination team has paid close attention to this vaccination work and has made every effort to ensure that the people are vaccinated and achieve the vaccination plan as determined by the Royal Government.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that "all the members of the army keep this work as a big task for them and he considers this vaccination work to be a great merit building for the people." "So he worked hard, no matter how hard it was in the rain, the wind, the thunder, no matter how tired he was, how hard they tried to get the vaccine to reach the people."
In addition to the vaccination process in the four southwestern provinces, the Ministry of Defense's vaccination team has been tasked with providing vaccinations in Svay Rieng and Kampong Cham provinces. According to General Ith Sarath, in these two provinces, the army provided more than 170,000 people.
Under all circumstances, such as disasters and hardships, the military is seen as a major driving force for the government, such as vaccination.
Vaccinated residents praised the military's attitude towards vaccination and the friendly and gentle nature of the vaccinated population.
