The commitment of the Supreme Leader of the Cambodian People's Party was made in a message on June 28, 2021 to celebrate the 70th anniversary of the founding of the Cambodian People's Party (June 28, 1951).
Through this message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded of the success of the Cambodian People's Party in all previous elections in accordance with the principles of multi-party liberal democracy at both the national and sub-national levels, which is a clear testament to the people's trust. Strongly support the Cambodian People's Party in leading the country in the right way that brings peace, stability, prosperity and happiness of the people.
On behalf of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, Samdech expressed his deepest gratitude to his compatriots everywhere in the country and abroad who have seen the truth of the party's leadership and provided justice and support. Shake the party in all circumstances, make the party able to serve the nation and the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "In response to this trust, the Party will continue to do everything in its power to defend national independence and sovereignty, maintain peace, political stability, security and macroeconomic stability, and strengthen democracy." "Promote social harmony and promote economic development, improve people's lives to be more prosperous."
The Cambodian People's Party, which has been in power through elections for six terms, was formed on June 28, 1951, with the original name of the Khmer Revolutionary People's Party, which originated from the patriotic movement of the Cambodian people. Against the colonists for national independence.
In its great achievements, after joining the opposition to foreign colonization and domination, this populist party overthrew the Pol Pot genocidal regime on January 7, 1979, and later reunited the nation and Restore Cambodia leading to complete peace.
(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, announced the launch of the Kovid 19 vaccination campaign to people in four districts from June 29, 2021 onwards, as the vaccines have already arrived in Kampong Cham. This announcement was made during the distribution of gifts to 100 Christian families on the morning of June 28, 2021 at the Boeung Kok Pagoda, Sangkat Boeung Kok, Kampong Cham.
Provincial Governor Un Chanda said that from tomorrow, the Kampong Cham provincial administration will launch a campaign to vaccinate 19 people in four districts: Kampong Siem, Prey Chhor, Cheung Prey and Batheay.
The provincial governor confirmed that 19 free Kovid vaccines have been delivered to the Kampong Cham provincial administration, and the medical team has already prepared for the vaccination.
The provincial governor also invited residents living in the town, market vendors and government officials to be vaccinated against Kovid 19 according to the goals set by the doctors and do not forget to bring their ID cards. .
He recalled that so far in Kampong Cham province, there are 47,000 families living in poverty due to the Kovid 19 crisis. At the same time, the Royal Government has also launched a cash subsidy program for people who fall into poverty in the context of 19 cases of Kovid, with a total amount of more than 20 million dollars so far.
