BREAKING: The Ministry of Health urges people to strengthen the implementation of measures to prevent the transmission of 19 new Kovid virus
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 28, 2021, the Ministry of Health issued a press release on strengthening the implementation of measures to prevent the transmission of 19 Kovid virus (including new mutations), especially individuals who need to participate properly. And serious. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News.
The vaccine is a tool that can reduce serious illness, hospitalization and mortality, the ministry said. But what scientists have learned is that due to the lack of proper and rigorous implementation of personal protective measures, especially the high risk when mobile individuals travel from home to one place, forgetting to apply protective measures. Self or not implement consistently and sharply take self-defense measures.
Currently, the Ministry observes that individuals are forgetful, which causes the implementation of individual protection measures to be lax, especially in urban areas.
Therefore, the participation of all people plays an important role to protect themselves, their families and their communities and others to live safely and be able to maintain a livelihood by being able to make a living. This means that all citizens demand the implementation of:
* 3 protection: 1: Wear a mask: Especially when wearing a mask, do not touch the face of the mask or pull the mask under the chin and change the mask when it is wet 2: Wash your hands often with soap for a while. 40 seconds or with alcohol for 20 seconds 3: Keep a personal safety distance of one and a half meters or more: Even if you have family members, relatives who have a different home than you or close friends.
* 3 Do not: 1: Do not go to crowded places in this sense, including gatherings, drinking as a family, relatives who live in a house other than you or close friends 2: Do not go to a closed place with no ventilation 3 : Do not touch each other, do not shake hands, do not shoulder each other, even family members, relatives who live in a house different from you or close friends.
The implementation of the three measures must be taken seriously and the local authorities should promote the implementation of the three protections and the three measures better, along with monitoring and enforcing the law.
The Ministry of Health would like to express its deep gratitude to all the people for their attention in preventing the transmission of Kovid-19 virus, and also call on the public to follow the above guidelines. Highly effective to contribute to cutting off the transmission of Kovid-19 virus and transmission of Code-19 virus from one person to another, especially to help prevent the transmission of new mutated viruses in Cambodia.
