The Sinovak vaccine, which arrived in Cambodia this morning, is the fifth dose of the 5 million doses that arrived in Cambodia in June.
Vaccination is a strategic solution of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19. As of June 26, Cambodia has received a total of 10 million doses of vaccines, both grants and orders.
Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister and Secretary of State for the Ministry of Economy and Finance, said that Cambodia will receive 20 million doses of the vaccine by August 2021. In July and August, a total of 9 million doses of the vaccine arrived in Cambodia in a row.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth pointed out that the arrival of the vaccine was faster than planned by Cambodia. According to Mr. Vongsy Visoth, Cambodia originally expected 20 million doses of the vaccine to be available by the end of the year or early 2022.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that the success of the vaccine depends on two main factors, including Samdech Techo's personal efforts to find a strategy, and the other is Samdech Techo's individual. A person whom the Chinese government values and has good relations with.
Through the presence of vaccines that arrived before the plan, Mr. Vongsey Visoth said that the Royal Government will prepare a plan to vaccinate people as soon as possible. Mr. Vongsey Visoth expressed the expectation that the vaccination will be completed by November or December 2021.
It should be noted that from February 10 to June 26, Cambodia vaccinated nearly 4 million people and foreigners living and working in Cambodia, equivalent to nearly 40 percent.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth said that the vaccination of the people as planned will help Cambodia to control the spread of Kovid 19 well, which is one of the reasons for Cambodia to achieve better economic conditions.
