As the death toll rose to nine on Sunday, relatives of the victims were "deeply saddened" by the news and even more concerned about the slowdown in rescue efforts. No one has been pulled from the rubble alive since last Thursday, hours after part of a 12-storey building collapsed.
Some family members of the victims were taken by bus on Sunday to a location near the scene after they expressed frustration with the speed of rescue efforts, demanding that authorities Allow them to wait at the scene and urge the authorities to bring in experts from other countries to help.
It should be noted that the collapsed condominium building above was reportedly built in 1981 with a total of 136 rooms and about 55 rooms collapsed. The cause of the accident has not been confirmed, while rescue efforts are ongoing.
