AIDS Healthcare Foundation to Hold Press Conference to Boost International Cooperation for Kovid-19 Vaccine
(Phnom Penh): The AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF) Cambodia will hold a press conference on June 30, 2021 through Zoom from 10:00 am to 11:30 am to demand Increasing international cooperation will increase the production of vaccines worldwide to fight Kovid-19.
The conference will feature public health experts and call for faster and global access to vaccines, and urge world leaders to support a proposal to suspend patents for Kovid-19 vaccine. And help increase vaccine production by companies in many countries around the world.
The AHF Cambodia press conference is an initiative of the "VOW" campaign, which is a campaign and advocacy activity in countries in Asia, Africa, Europe, Latin America and the United States.
The AHF Cambodia press conference will be attended by keynote speakers such as:
* Dr. Huy Sikheng, Country Manager, Cambodian AIDS Health Care Foundation, and shared the purpose of the campaign and the appeal to the global community
* Mr. Tim Vara, a representative of civil society organizations, and share his efforts to get vaccinated in the private and public interest.
* Mr. Sorn Sothearith, President of the Network of People Living with HIV in Cambodia and shared the campaign and activities, lessons learned from HIV and getting vaccinated together.
Miss VDnet, a singer and actress, will share her experiences as a 19-year-old Kovid infected and the bitter lessons of losing a beloved mother.
* Dr. Chhim Sarath, Regional Director for Asia and summarized the conference and the global call.
Kovid-19 has devastated lives around the world. Many families have lost loved ones and the death toll continues to rise in Asia and around the world.
