It should be reminded that in the past, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has increased this fund, especially for the cyclo riders, who have received many benefits, such as receiving a subsidy of 7,000 riels One day (every 10 days) Free medical treatment from public hospitals and other benefits such as big national holiday allowance and retirement.
(Pursat): Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province and Chairman of the Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes in Veal Veng District, warned the officials in charge of preventing and cracking down on natural resource crimes not to abuse their power or position. State land, if this is the case, the law will not pardon.
The provincial governor made the remarks while chairing a meeting to review the work of the Sub-Committee on Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes in Thmor Da Commune on June 26, 2021 at the Police Battalion Headquarters. Defend the land border No. 825.
The purpose of this meeting is to understand the challenges in the performance of the subcommittee and to guide all forces stationed along the border line to carry out their duties and responsibilities as defined by law, without taking power or role. To violate the state land, and if there is to return the land to the state, to avoid losing their role or leading to law enforcement.
On that occasion, Mr. Mao Thunin continued to inspect the location of the encroached land at the foot of 16 hills and to keep the location that the sub-committee has kept in the past and also visited the families of the 28 forces. Families benefited from the location of the land, maintaining the original condition and not to continue logging.
It should be noted that according to Article 3 of the Decision of Pursat Provincial Administration No. 061/20, dated October 26, 2020 on the establishment of the Provincial Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes in Veal Veng Sub-Committee. Workers have the following roles and responsibilities:
* Prevent and suppress the crime of encroachment on state forest land in the five communes.
* Search for information, identify the perpetrators and file a case according to legal procedures to the court.
* Educate local people to understand the law and the benefits of conserving natural resources.
* Report on the results achieved and challenges related to the implementation of work to the provincial committee.
