Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued, "According to the data, images and research results of the Ministry of Environment, Virachey National Park, the ASEAN Natural Heritage Park, is an area rich in biodiversity, including many rare species of wildlife. "It was filmed through an automatic camera, which the research team of the Department of Natural Conservation of the East Mekong River of the Ministry of Environment put in place for three months from March to May 2021."
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said that the study was to collect important data on the presence of wildlife and to organize the division of management areas within protected areas.
At the same time, Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that there are four management areas in the protected area: the core area, the conservation area, the sustainable use area and the community area, and the demarcation of the management area in the protected area with the participation of all stakeholders. The purpose is to clearly define the legal framework, technical management and based on the experience and best practices from countries in the region and the world.
These aim to ensure the effective and efficient management and conservation of protected area systems and biodiversity corridors, increase the living standards of local communities, reduce dependence on forest products, and ensure a balance between emissions and greenhouse gas emissions. From the forestry sector.
