The operation to confiscate the lion took place on the morning of June 27, 2021 in a villa located at 22, Street 306, Village 7, Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, where a Chinese man raised a male lion. Wildlife species in the home illegally.
Phnom Penh Prey Chey Administration Director said, "Because some neighbors reported raising lions in the back of the villa by a Chinese man, the authorities cooperated with the local authorities to conduct a search. "Take one of the lions to be sent for safekeeping."
He added that people do not have the right to raise wild animals, which is a rare species, which is contrary to the law and Article 49 of the Law on Forestry, paragraph 2, point 3, which states that the ownership of inventory or care. Keeping zoos or families as endangered species is prohibited.
"A male lion will be handed over to the Phnom Tamao Wildlife Conservation and Rescue Center for further rearing," he said. "The Chinese owners have been called in by the authorities to stop raising such wildlife."
It should be noted that the male lion weighs more than 70 kilograms and has been raised by Chinese men since he was a child until he was about a year and a half old, eating about 6 kilograms of raw meat a day.
Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: Planting seedlings in addition to natural wood to create greenery, increase forest cover and adapt to climate change
(Kampong Speu): "The participation of the people in collecting tree seeds, planting trees, not only to create greenery, increase forest cover and adapt to climate change, but the trees you planted now will become "Forests and natural heritage for your descendants and also part of the future tourist attraction."
Secretary of State of the Ministry of Environment Net Pheaktra, on behalf of the Ministry of Environment, praised the work of Cambodian youth as well as the community in participating in the protection and conservation of natural resources honestly and upholding national interests and community interests.
He stressed that this is a joint effort to increase greenery in the community and to participate in the conservation of natural resources.
The senior official added that the Ministry of Environment continues to encourage people, youth and volunteers to take care of the environment, forest, wildlife and natural resources honestly and on the basis of good cooperation. Common interests and do not use the environment and natural resources as an excuse to take action that embodies any corrupt political agenda.
He said that these activities are also to make people stop entering the forest, cut down trees, stop entering the forest to hunt animals as before and turn to participate in forest conservation to protect natural resources and prepare their community into a tourist area. Nature is attractive and left for future generations. He added that this is an activity that is encouraged and supported.
Mr. Tan Kimsour, the initiator of the Earth Wound Treatment Campaign, expressed his pleasure with the direct visits and encouragement from the leaders of the Ministry and the Department of Environment and the provision of incentives to buy delicious food. People living in this area.
He added that the research found that in Africa, Thailand and some other countries in the world, they use the soil to plant seeds, they use a short time and have a high efficiency. In Africa, up to 8 million saplings can be planted per year, all of which is a good experience to apply in Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Tan Kimsour said that this project has the support and encouragement of the Ministry of Environment and the support of the administration of Kampong Speu, which always provides direct cooperation in support of youth activities that participate in protection. And constantly conserve natural resources. This past activity has changed the minds of many people, especially those who used to be loggers and loggers.
Mr. Tan Kimsour offered to work as a forest protection worker with a decent salary and they started to love nature.
He stressed that the campaign to plant trees is only a small part, what is important is to participate in cultivating the spirit of the people, some of whom never understand, never know, never interested in the importance of the forest to turn to participate in caring together. .
According to Mr. Tan Kimsour, the project to plant seeds to treat the wounds of the earth is with the participation of young volunteers, Green Vera.
Mr. Pen Chamrong, an artist who volunteered for this work, said that as citizens as well as artists have a role to play in protecting natural resources, so to change the mindset of our people, we must start ourselves first. . He added that although he was busy with his art work, he had to take time to participate in all of this work, which was a source of pride for him and his family.
A resident who was paralyzed in both legs due to a traffic accident during the construction work who participated in this work confirmed that he worked here through Mr. Tan Kim Sour to work, while other places do not work because he is disabled Both legs.
He added that the work of cultivating the land to plant the seeds per day earns 30,000 riel, which has contributed a lot to support the expenses in the daily life of his family. Raising the soil to plant the seeds is a good job, it will contribute to the preservation of natural resources together.
