The following is the content of Mr. HUN Many's congratulations:
Please remember that in the Democratic Kampuchea regime, people have no rights at all because their daily lives are under threat, forced to work overtime, lose their families and live in fear all the time. In the most dangerous and unbearable situations in some areas, patriotic movements have rallied to form the "Kampuchean United Front for National Salvation" to oppose the overthrow of this vicious regime.
Through history, it has become clear that the CPP has gone through countless hardships in its activities and movements, both during the period of independence from the French colonies, the liberation of the people and the country from massacre. Under the Pol Pot regime, the country was restored from scratch and full territorial unification (win-win politics).
In all those difficult stages, we always see the presence of Cambodian elite warriors who fought for their lives, sacrificing their flesh and blood, wisdom and spirit as capital to raise the flag of national unity for the sole purpose of thinking about the nation and the people. People are a priority.
The Cambodian People's Party has gone through countless difficult histories, but the Cambodian People's Party has always been with the people in all circumstances, both at a time when the country is in a difficult situation and in leading the country to continuous development.
Due to the factors of peace, Cambodia has built a society with independence, sovereignty, democracy, peace, harmony and complete freedom for the people.
Moreover, the factor of peace has created an environment to attract foreign investment to Cambodia, which promotes continuous economic growth and improves the living standards of the people from day to day. Days.
The lessons of history have already been shown, when peace is lost, when national unity, internal unity is shattered, when the common sense is disturbed, which causes the outside world to take the opportunity to exacerbate the situation. Create a division of forces within the country that could cause the nation to fall into the flames of civil war in the blink of an eye.
