(Phnom Penh): Deputy Director General Se Sokhorn, Representative of Dr. Kun Nhim, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, led a delegation from the General Department of Customs and Excise of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to attend the group meeting. The 138th International Customs Cooperation Council, organized by the World Customs Organization (WCO) via video.
The meeting heard reports and discussions focused on: 1. Capacity building 2. Customs technical work, such as rules of origin, tariffs, and classification of goods, 3. Compliance and trade facilitation, and 4. Budget and Finance of the World Customs Organization. The meeting also noted the current status of the implementation of the WCO Covid-19 Action Plan, which contains 25 activities that are useful for members to consider and implement.
As a result, the meeting approved a number of important tasks, such as: 1. Necessary technical documents and guidelines related to the implementation of the WCO 2022 Tariff Schedule 2. Guidelines on Disaster Management and Supply Chain 3. SAFE FoS Standard Framework 2021 and decided on the budget recommendations of the Finance Committee, which can facilitate the Secretariat to continue to work to provide quality services to members.
