Samdech Tea Banh: On behalf of the ASEAN Defense Ministers, Cambodia wants to see the people of the region live in freedom and transparency
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, confirmed to Mr. KISHI Nobuo, Minister of Defense of Japan, that on behalf of the ASEAN Defense Ministers, Cambodia continues to maintain a common aspiration and desire to see the people of the region. Can live with freedom, transparency, harmonious environment and the ability to compete.
"As a member of the ASEAN Defense Ministers, Cambodia continues to maintain a common aspiration and desire to see the people of the region live in freedom, transparency, a harmonious environment and the ability to compete," he said.
Samdech Tea Sena Tea Banh emphasized that the building of the ASEAN Community under the concept of "Free and Open Indo-Pacific" is very important in building a free and open region through the promotion of a multilateral system. Proclaim and respect the law to ensure the security, peace and prosperity of the region, avoid interference or political service of any country that is not in accordance with the intentions and does not serve the interests of the people of the community as a whole.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh emphasized that Cambodia encourages stakeholders to resolve regional issues by respecting and adhering to the principles of international law, non-interference, respecting the way of life, culture, tradition and history, which are the values of each country. The goal is to strengthen the values of peace, dignity and unity.
"Cambodia supports the five ASEAN mechanisms and welcomes the" Free and Open Indo-Pacific "initiative, which is free, open, environmental and transparent," he said.
During the talks, the two sides considered that today's talks are very important in strengthening the friendly relations and bilateral cooperation between the two Ministries of Defense of Cambodia and Japan, aimed at enhancing the capacity of national defense and political security. Including humanitarian through training human resources to have the ability to contribute to building closer and deeper military ties between the two countries.
