(Phnom Penh): According to the image data collected from the automatic cameras that the Ministry of Environment officials have placed in the protected areas in the eastern highlands and the Central Cardamom Mountains have found the presence of wild dogs. Although not yet abundant, this is good news for conservatives and environmentalists.
He said that over the past few months, wild dogs have been photographed by self-portraits in Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary in Pursat Province and in Virachey National Park in Ratanakkiri Province.
The spokesman said that in addition to the Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary in the Central Cardamom Mountains and Virachey National Park, the presence of wild dogs in other wildlife sanctuaries in the eastern highlands, such as the sanctuary. Sre Pok Forest, Phnom Prech Wildlife Sanctuary and Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary, etc., through the automatic camera captured images of these species, including young children.
"This is a good sign of biodiversity in Cambodia, where rare species such as wild dogs are beginning to appear in some areas and in some areas," Neth Pheaktra said.
