Phnom Penh Capital Administration is restoring two main canals on both sides of National Road 4 and Railway and plans to build a road on the back of the canal
(Phnom Penh): With great consideration for the flooding in the western part of Phnom Penh, Governor Khuong Sreng ordered the Phnom Penh Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to continue the inspection of Kampoul and Por Senchey districts. Rehabilitate some major canals to relieve flooding to avoid flooding of villages during the rainy season.
Mr. Mao Bunthoeun, Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Phnom Penh, said on the afternoon of June 25 that two main canals on either side of the railway from National Road 4 connected to O'Lao Canal to open the water to flow. Kob Srov Dam Lake. The canal plays an important role in relieving flooding in the western part of Phnom Penh, especially in the territory of the entire Kambol district and part of Por Sen Chey district.
Mr. Mao Bunthoeun said that the rehabilitation of the two main canals was carried out after receiving an order from the Governor of Phnom Penh, then the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology cooperated with the district authorities to rehabilitate and plan to complete in time. Short ahead.
He added that the main canal on the west side of the railway was being rehabilitated in 12 meters and 4 meters deep, while the canal on the east side of the railway was being rehabilitated. The canal is 6 meters long and 4 meters deep.
He said that this was originally an old main canal, but was dredged by the influx of rubbish and weeds for many years until the entire canal was wiped out and water could not flow through here. Boeung Tumnup Kob Srov causes the flooding of residential infrastructure in the western part of Phnom Penh every year, especially in the territory of Khan Kambol and part of Por Sen Chey district.
He added that after the two main canals reopen, it will have the role of releasing rainwater from Ang Snoul district of Kandal province, Kambol district and Por Sen Chey district. He expects that this year's rainy season will help reduce flooding caused by heavy rains west of Phnom Penh.
Mr. Khim Sunsoda, Governor of Kambol District, confirmed that next year, after the rehabilitation of these two canals, the Kambol District Administration plans to submit a proposal to the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to clear the back of the canal to make way for the people. The process is especially able to relieve traffic congestion from National Road 4.
