More than 7,000 liters of counterfeit alcohol or methanol were cracked down on by the General Department of PPR in Po Sen Chey district
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of June 24, 2021, officials of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud "KPR" with the permission of the Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and In collaboration with the local authority of Po Sen Chey district, they raided a place to store and distribute counterfeit alcohol or methanol with an address in Sangkat Choam Chao 2.
During the inspection, the experts took samples suspected to be counterfeit alcohol and immediately analyzed them by the mobile laboratory vehicle of the General Department of KPR, with the following results:
121 cans of suspected alcohol and 800 bottles of 4,030 liters of methanol (counterfeit alcohol) were found * 104 cans of suspected alcohol, equivalent to 3,120 liters of methanol (counterfeit alcohol) were found.
After the inspection, the professional officers took the samples of the products and analyzed them in the laboratory of the General Department of KPRP. To confirm additional results. All exhibits are stored in a closed enclosure and temporarily closed at the waiting area for further proceedings.
