Samdech Techo Hun Sen recommends six points to further enhance the effectiveness of the fight against drugs (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the occasion of the International Day Against Drug Abuse on June 26 2021 recommends six points to further enhance the effectiveness and efficiency of anti-drug work during the 19 epidemic period.
* First, the National Authority for Combating Drugs and the Command of the Campaign Against Illegal Drugs, as well as the relevant ministries, institutions and relevant units must continue to pay attention to responsible owners and implement them more effectively. Its role and responsibilities are the 6th plan to fight against illegal drugs that the Royal Government has recently launched.
Adopting "3, 3, 3" measures and other health measures to help prevent and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease in the workplace, on themselves, their families and communities.
* Second, the Commission in charge of education shall continue to urge the relevant ministries, institutions, capital-provincial drug control committees, factories, enterprises to educate and disseminate the dangers of drugs, especially through the media and social media. Conjugation context 19.
At the same time, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports must continue to guide and guide educational institutions at all levels to find all ways to continue to disseminate education on both the drug problem and the problem of the spread of Kovid 19 to students on a regular basis. Make them aware and have a sufficient basis to protect themselves and continue to educate friends, family and others in the community.
The first report is to report to the authorities about the drug problem that we know. At the same time, parents and guardians must continue to be encouraged to pay more attention and participate in educating their children not to be involved in drug problems or to educate and encourage their children who are involved or addicted to drugs to stop and go. Get treatment and rehabilitation in a timely manner.
* Fourth: The Committee in charge of the treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts and the Capital and Provincial Drug Control Committees must continue to strengthen the capacity and quality of treatment and rehabilitation of drug addicts, both at health facilities and in Temporary centers to ensure the quality and effectiveness of treatment and rehabilitation services for drug addicts.
In addition, in the circumstances of the spread of Kovid 19 must be carefully considered and appropriate measures to ensure the effectiveness of prevention and control of the spread of Kovid 19 in the goal of providing treatment and rehabilitation services for drug addicts. Addicted.
