Ministry of Social Affairs Announces Child Protection Information Management System in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, with the participation of UNICEF USAID and the European Union, on June 25, 2021, announced the launch of the Child Protection Information Management System in Cambodia.
This child protection information management system is very important, allowing ministries, institutions, service providers, development agencies, NGOs, information seekers and the public to download information on the progress of child protection services and valuable data to use in Policy making, action plans, and evaluation reports are intended to provide support and protection to all children of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
During the launch, Mr. Nim Thoth, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Social Affairs, stated that this is another new achievement in strengthening the child protection information management system and highlighting the efforts of the Royal Government and relevant NGOs in Implement action plans to improve child care in families and integrate 30% of children from child care centers to safe families.
At the same time, Mr. Nim Thoth also thanked UNICEF USAID and the European Union for providing both technical and financial support in drafting these documents until today.
It should be noted that the child protection information management system in Cambodia has 50 indicators of 5 core sectors related to child protection under the jurisdiction of 13 ministries and 2 partner organizations.
