Senior Minister Kun Kim Instructs Capital-Provincial Governors to Prepare for Flood Disaster
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, instructed the Capital-Provincial Governors to be ready to respond to the upcoming floods.
In a letter sent to the capital-provincial governor on June 25, 2021, Senior Minister Kun Kim emphasized that heavy rainfall will fall in the catchment area of the Mekong and Tonle Sap rivers, which could cause river flooding. Jump up.
According to the weather factors at the beginning of the rainy season in 2021, Mr. Kun Kim advised the Disaster Management Committee of the Capital, Province, Municipality, District, Khan, Commune and Sangkat to pay the highest attention and be prepared in advance.
Mr. Kun Kim further advised that in the event of a disaster, the competent authorities located at the scene must conduct emergency operations in response to the disaster before the operation team of the Capital and Provincial Disaster Management Committee arrives.
At the same time, the Secretariat of the Capital and Provincial Disaster Management Committee shall coordinate the response in the event of a disaster, collect and analyze information through the Presem system and provide action to the Chairman of the Capital and Provincial Disaster Management Committee and report regularly to the National Committee for Disaster Management.
Senior Minister Kun Kim expressed his strong hope for a high sense of responsibility and strong cooperation from the Disaster Management Committee at all levels to ensure the safety and well-being of the people.
