So does this mean that North Korea really does not want to negotiate with the United States? North Korean observers believe Pyongyang still wants to meet with the United States to seek international assistance and the easing of sanctions to save the deteriorating national economy. The perception comes after Kim Jong Un himself recently acknowledged that his country was facing a food crisis caused by COVID-19 and typhoons.
However, more importantly, with or without negotiations, there is little expectation that North Korea will give up or stop developing nuclear weapons. That is, the talks are just a way to maintain relations with North Korea and ease tensions on the Korean Peninsula.
* Why did North Korea choose nuclear weapons?
Under Kim Jong Un, North Korea tested a number of missiles and nuclear weapons until US military experts claimed that Pyongyang now has ICBMs equipped with nuclear warheads, such as the Hwasong-15, capable of firing. To the United States, with 20 to 60 nuclear warheads and even the ability to produce six nuclear bombs a year.
(Stung Treng): The Stung Treng Provincial Administration announced the discovery of 19 cases of Kovid at the location of "Galaxy" restaurant in Sre Po village, Srah Russey commune, Stung Treng city on June 24, 2021.
