In a video released last week, the ambassador noted that the rainy season has arrived in Cambodia. The rainy season often causes sewage congestion and flooding in Phnom Penh.
The ambassador said one of the main reasons for the blockage was improper dumping. Improper dumping can also cause some rubbish to flow into the river.
The ambassador emphasized that the Royal Government is currently assisting Cambodia in the project to rehabilitate the drainage system and provide technical assistance to prevent plastic from flowing into the sea.
