Mr. Mikami Masahiro also called on the Cambodian people to develop a good attitude in life, and he emphasized the educational phrase, "Your actions today will make life better in the future."
(Phnom Penh): FUNCINPEC Party on June 24, 2021 strongly condemned the prisoner Sam Rainsy, a rebel movement, who once again posted an insulting message to the King. The royalist party also called on the judiciary to take strong action to bring the illegal rebel leader to justice.
FUNCINPEC's outspoken sentencing comes after the outlawed rebel leader Sam Rainsy cut off the power of the King, a revered figure of the Cambodian people across the country, and used abusive language on June 22, 2021.
FUNCINPEC considers the content published by Sam Rainsy to be public on Facebook as a serious insult and has seriously damaged the reputation of His Majesty the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Most of our Cambodian people have violated the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia, Chapter 2, Article 7, which states that "the King can not be violated by anyone."
FUNCINPEC considers Sam Rainsy's repeated dark accusations against the King of Cambodia with malicious intent to serve the political ambitions of revenge against the monarchy and the throne, which FUNCINPEC as well as The royalists, Sihanoukists and the Khmer people could not accept it.
It should be noted that Sam Rainsy, the leader of the extremist opposition group, was sentenced to four years in prison in June 2019 for insulting the King.
In connection with this case, on September 16, 2019, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court issued an order for all levels of authorities to investigate and bring Sam Rainsy to justice for insulting the King.
