Factors that can help reduce poverty and improve the quality of life of the concessionaire, because the LASED III project not only provides land, not only social land concessions for housing to the poor, but also provides Social land concessions for growing crops as well.
In addition, the LASED III social land concession and economic development project, with global credit and the Government of Cambodia, has also trained people in agriculture, animal husbandry, vegetable breeding, market marketing, schools, health centers, and irrigation infrastructure. Such as training people to save money and provide funding for community development, which is a necessary capital for agriculture and handicrafts.
The Minister of Land Management added that the special feature of the LASED III Land Allocation, Social Affairs and Economic Development Project is to take into account the livelihoods of indigenous peoples. The project will provide a budget to support indigenous community land registration, land preparation for community forestry, and commune land use planning, which are essential tools for comprehensive and sustainable development.
It should be noted that the LASED III Social Land Concession and Economic Development Project is a project of the Royal Government with a total budget of $ 107 million, of which the World Bank loan is $ 93 million and the Royal Government contribution is $ 14 million. The project must be implemented by the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries within 6 years from October 2020 to December 2026.
The project covers a total of 71 locations, including 26 sites for social land concessions and 45 locations for indigenous communities with a total area of 30,000 hectares, of which 10 are indigenous communities. There are a total of 6,500 families, of which 1,500 are indigenous communities.
The LASED III Social Land Concession and Economic Development project focuses on five areas, including: social land concessions, indigenous community land registration, commune land use planning, and system development. Physical infrastructure and support for the livelihood development of project beneficiaries. Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon Receives French Ambassador
