By: Chao Chak Smok, Phnom Penh, June 23, 2021 The Cambodian government declares its support for Britain as an ASEAN dialogue partner.
The confirmation of Cambodia's support was made by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, during a bilateral meeting with Dominic Raab, Minister of Foreign Affairs and Development of the United Kingdom. On the morning of June 23, 2021, during a one-day visit by a British diplomat to Cambodia.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs claims that within the framework of ASEAN, Mr. Prak Sokhon informed Mr. Dominic Raab on Cambodia's preparations for the ASEAN Chairmanship in 2022, focusing on the promotion of ASEAN Centrality and Unity. Accelerate recovery after the effects of Kovid-19 and improve public welfare.
"His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister commended the United Kingdom for its deep interest in establishing a Dialogue Partnership with ASEAN, and reaffirmed Cambodia's support for the United Kingdom's request by the United Kingdom. "Britain has always had an active relationship with ASEAN."
The two Foreign Ministers also exchanged views on a number of regional and international issues of common interest and concern, including the draft Code of Conduct for the parties in the South China Sea, joint efforts for the return. Towards normalization of Myanmar and the fight against climate change, focusing on the use of renewable energy and without compromising the ecosystems and technologies that play an important role.
In connection with this, Mr. Prak Sokhon announced that the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will lead a high-level delegation to attend the 26th United Nations Conference on Climate Change (COP26) in Glasgow. The two foreign ministers agreed to continue working closely together in both the regional and international frameworks.
