The United Kingdom, which left the EU at the end of December last year, has decided to continue to provide preferential treatment to Cambodia, effective January 1, 2021, after seeing the worsening of the 19-post Kovid crisis after the EU. Europe has decided to remove the EBA from about 20% of all goods imported from Cambodia.
During the bilateral meeting, the two foreign ministers agreed on the importance of dialogue on trade issues. The two Foreign Ministers shared a common goal to further strengthen and expand bilateral relations and cooperation in a number of areas for mutual benefit, especially in the fields of economy, trade, education and demining. Health and environment.
It should be noted that Dominic Rahab arrived in Cambodia on the night of June 22, 2021 for a one-day official visit to further promote and strengthen bilateral relations between the two countries and be a step forward. In multilateral cooperation within the ASEAN framework.
