MOSCOW (Reuters) - The black market in the issuance of fake vaccination certificates is booming in Russia after Moscow authorities ordered all public officials to be vaccinated against Kovid 19; This is according to the release by Reuters on Wednesday night, June 23, 2021.
It is easy to find advertisements for the issuance of illegal fake certificates on telegrams, as these messengers target Russians who are not vaccinated but want to keep their jobs while the cost of issuing certificates These are growing rapidly and demand seems to be on the rise.
Moscow and many parts of Russia have taken drastic measures to encourage people to get vaccinated, as new cases in the country have risen alarmingly, blamed on the virus. New Delta.
The Kremlin has warned that people who have not been vaccinated against Kovid 19 will not be able to work in all workplaces in Russia and could be discriminated against.
