(Pursat): Pursat Provincial Governor Mr. Mao Thunin has been paying close attention to the construction of houses, infrastructure and electricity network for veterans in "Bun Rany Sen Chey Damnak Troyeung" village, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district.
So far, about 105 houses donated by the Cambodian Red Cross have been completed, while another 25 houses are under construction in Area A on 150 projects in the second phase.
In addition to the construction of houses, the team of the Veterans Association and the provincial authorities have been preparing to build health centers, schools, as well as some plans for officials to speed up the construction of infrastructure.
Mr. Mao Thunin, as the Provincial Governor and the Honorary President of the Pursat Veterans Association, paid close attention to the construction work to be completed quickly to the veterans as directed by Samdech Kittipritthbandit. Bun Rany Hun Sen.
It should be noted that the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to provide land at the above location to about 628 families of veterans in Pursat province, with each family receiving 70 meters by 150 meters of land (housing and agricultural land).
Along with the Royal Government providing land, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, as well as philanthropists, helped to build houses for the needy and disabled veterans of these 628 families. Currently, 105 houses have been built, of which 50 houses were handed over - received the first step on June 12, 2021.
Veterans and their families who have come to live in their completed homes are confident and committed to building a new life with hope, happiness and beautiful weather forever.
