(Prey Veng): The groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng Vocational Training Center was held at Chea Sim Kamchay Mear University, Prey Veng Province on the morning of June 22, 2021.
The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Touch Visal Sok, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Vice Chairman of the Board of Directors of Chea Sim Kamchay Mear University, Representative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports General Department of Logistics and Finance, Ministry of Interior, represented by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and was attended by local authorities, management and a total of 35 students.
This historic achievement is a gift from Prince Sar Kheng and was led by General Chhorn Sarane with the aim of contributing to human resource development and providing opportunities for lower secondary school graduates in Kamchay Mear district and other areas across the country to continue their education. Technical and vocational education in all specialties from level 1, 2, 3 and 4 to contribute to the development of Kamchay Mear and surrounding districts, as well as society as a whole.
The ceremony took place in the order of tradition, with the preparation of the Krong Pali ceremony for good fortune, good luck, good luck, success, hitting the foundation as a symbol and a friendly atmosphere with a solemn atmosphere, joy, intimacy and extreme pride. Analysis: South Vietnam casts shadow over US troop withdrawal from Afghanistan
In a statement issued last Sunday, the White House stated that in the first face-to-face meeting, Biden would reassure Ghani and Abdullah of US commitment and support to the people of Afghanistan. Including diplomacy, economics, and humanitarian aid, and the US president will reaffirm his commitment to ensure that Afghanistan does not become a haven for terrorists or illegal armed groups.
But this Friday's meeting is not expected to change Joe Biden's decision to withdraw US troops from Afghanistan.
At first glance, the number of troops is small, but combined with Afghan government forces, they are strong enough to fight more than 3,000 Taliban militants and 7,000 less active militants. Others. By comparison, Nixon withdrew 69,000 US troops from South Vietnam, knowing that North Vietnam had more than 150,000 troops along the South Vietnamese border, including the Viet Cong communist army.
After the complete withdrawal of US troops, Saigon fell into the hands of the North Vietnamese communists in 1975, and a year later the whole of South Vietnam officially fell into the hands of North Vietnam. Most historians do not understand that the United States lost the war in Vietnam by force, but the United States lost for domestic political reasons: most Americans did not support the war in Vietnam or Indochina.
In fact, according to most experts, the Taliban will expand its control of territory in southern and eastern Afghanistan, where the militant group is active. The Taliban has vowed not to attack the United States, but has not vowed to attack Kabul.
With the help of US airstrikes, Afghan government forces were able to defend many cities, but without US intervention, continued control of the remaining cities or territories would not be possible. The first city that could fall into the hands of the Taliban could be Kandahar, which is already under siege by the militants.
The Taliban is not completely in control of Afghanistan. That is, those who ruled Kabul were in control of Afghanistan, so Kabul could be their next target when the United States withdraws its troops. But the biggest concern is the fear that a civil war could erupt soon if there is an internal split within the Kabul government.
US officials under Joe Biden do not believe that the Afghan government will collapse immediately after the US withdrawal. On the other hand, they also believe that Biden will also not allow the Taliban to do whatever they want, while there is speculation that the United States may continue to keep a small task force to help. Government of Afghanistan. But the rest of the decision rests with Biden himself.
