WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States has agreed to lift all sanctions on Iran's oil and transportation, as well as remove some high-ranking officials from the blacklist to restore its 2015 nuclear deal, Iranian officials said on Wednesday. Tehran with the superpowers now suspended. This is according to the release by The Arab News on Wednesday night, June 23, 2021.
Under the 2015 nuclear deal, Iran agreed to restrict its nuclear program in exchange for lifting international sanctions. Three years later, former US President Donald Trump abandoned the deal and re-imposed sanctions as Tehran responded by violating some nuclear sanctions.
The new US administration, led by President Joe Biden, intends to reinstate the agreement, but the two sides have not yet agreed on any steps.
