June 23, 2021 is the second day of the 19 Kovid vaccination operations in four provinces in southwestern Cambodia: Sihanoukville, Koh Kong, Kampong Speu and Takeo. On June 22, the first day of the vaccination operation in the four provinces, the immunization team of the Ministry of National Defense vaccinated nearly 60,000 people.
This morning, June 23, 2021, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Joint Chief of Staff of the 19-Kovid Vaccination Operation of the Ministry of National Defense, who is monitoring the vaccination process in Sihanoukville, said: People in the provinces are more aware of the value and benefits of vaccines in protecting health as well as fighting Kovid 19.
He claimed that many people have volunteered to get vaccinated by local authorities.
According to Ith Sarath, it is hoped that on June 23, more people will be vaccinated in the four provinces than yesterday. He also urged residents who receive the vaccine to listen to the authorities' arrangements and to avoid congregations that could lead to the spread of Kovid 19.
According to General Ith Sarath, according to the four provincial plans, a total of 1,244,000 people will be vaccinated. But the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces is tasked with vaccinating 810,000 people.
He also confirmed that the Army Vaccination Team is working to complete the first dose in the four provinces between June 22 and 30, 2021.
