Cambodian Students Association of China and Bank of China co-organize an online seminar on financial services for study in China
(Phnom Penh): The Bank of China (Hong Kong) Phnom Penh Branch, together with the Cambodian Students Association in China, organized an online seminar on financial services for study in China under the theme "10 advantages of continuing Study in China.
This online workshop was attended by about 200 parents and students from different high schools and universities across Cambodia.
Also at the seminar, Liu Xiaowei, Deputy Director of the Digital Finance Department for Individuals, presented the benefits of studying in China and how to find a suitable financial package and educational institution before leaving to study abroad. .
Mr. Oum Vuthy, Founder and Honorary President of the Cambodian Students Association in China, together with student representatives in China, shared his experiences of studying in China and solving challenges during his studies abroad. Also, the participants raised questions related to opening a bank account, money transfer services, choosing an educational institution and applying for a scholarship, and the answers were given to the participants in detail.
Ms. Elsie Gung, Assistant Country Director, Bank of China (Hong Kong) Phnom Penh Branch, shared her many years of overseas experience with the importance of rich life experience for personal development.
She believes that the bank will be a long-term partner in providing comprehensive banking services when international students start their business in Cambodia. She also encouraged students to join the Bank of China after returning to Cambodia to continue to contribute more to the local banking sector.
The workshop not only creates a new platform for students studying in China, but also allows them to better understand the various financial products and services that they will need while studying abroad. A good and reliable foundation for living abroad.
