Vaccination campaign in Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to provide health protection against Kovid 19
(Preah Sihanouk): Under the care of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the active coordination of the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration, the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has launched a campaign to vaccinate workers against 19 measles. Employees on June 22, 2021 ago.
Vaccination measures for all workers in the SEZ will further protect the lives and health of everyone, creating an immune barrier in the Sihanoukville SEZ to ensure normal production and operation. Of enterprises in the region.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Chief of Joint Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Vaccination Campaign Operations, and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Sihanoukville Province, accompanied by Mr. Cao JianJiang, Director General of SEZ Company, inspected the site. Advise on organizing order and having a friendly conversation.
Both General Ith Sarath, the provincial governor and the leaders of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone have expressed their full support for vaccinations in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone to ensure that workers in the area can be vaccinated. Kovid's disease 19.
Vaccination sites are in order and vaccinations are carried out sequentially. Vaccination staff waited quietly in the vaccination booth, kept a distance of one meter, and entered the information desk in a row of eight people to verify the vaccination information. After the information is verified, the vaccination process begins.
Brigadier General Dr. Bun Phoeun Ry, Deputy Commander of the Honorary Troops, in charge of vaccination, said that according to the high recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, attention should be paid to vaccination in economic zones. Especially in Sihanoukville, by strictly respecting the principle of "3 do not 3 protect".
All employees in the SEZ are vaccinated free of charge for 14 days to protect their safety and life.
