Russian President Vladimir Putin said on Tuesday that NATO was undermining the security of Europe as a whole (Video inside) Tensions are rising and the risk of a new arms race is becoming a reality. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Tuesday night, June 22, 2021.
Putin made the remarks in an article published by the German weekly Die Zeit to mark the 80th anniversary of the start of the Soviet Union's patriotic war against Nazi Germany.
He stressed that Russia seeks to develop its relations with Europe. But the expanding influence of the North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO) toward the East has led to an increase in mistrust in Europe.
The Russian president pointed out that since 1999, 14 countries, including the former Soviet Union, have joined NATO, which has really shattered the hopes of a non-divisive continent.
"The whole post-World War II history of Europe proves that the prosperity and security of our common continent is possible through the joint efforts of all countries, including Russia," he wrote.
