He confirmed that the three suspects who were arrested were: first, 21-year-old Mong Sambath, second, 19-year-old Mong Seiha (a sibling) and third, 19-year-old Dim Pros, alias Reach. Year of living in Khnar Tong village, Komarachea commune, Bati district, Takeo province. The victim, 27-year-old Maing Khemarak, suffered multiple injuries and a broken left wrist, causing his immediate death at the scene in front of the victim's house.
Authorities said the three suspects confessed that they had used a machete to stab the victim, Maing Khemarak, to death due to a verbal altercation while playing volleyball.
