Cambodia has been well implementing its commitment to support this Global Agreement Initiative:
1: Continue to strengthen the implementation more effectively and amend the labor law to meet the need to ensure better working conditions and harmony in industrial relations.
2. Strengthen the implementation of the Law on Trade Unions to ensure the rights and freedoms of professional organizations that represent the true voice and will of workers and employers to protect their legitimate rights and interests and be an effective dialogue partner. In social dialogue.
3. Strengthen the implementation of the Law on Minimum Wages as a strong legal framework for the sustainable protection of workers 'wages and ensure the use of democratic tripartite negotiation mechanisms to determine workers' minimum wages based on Scientific criteria for progress together.
4. Strengthen the mechanism for resolving labor disputes, both in the reconciliation phase of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and outside the judiciary, with the Arbitration Council aiming to ensure fairness, reduce challenges between employers and workers, as well as increase trust in A system of dispute resolution between stakeholders that further strengthens the culture of social dialogue.
5: Continue to strengthen the labor inspection mechanism to be more effective, transparent and credible from all stakeholders to ensure respect for working conditions and labor rights of workers and employers to prevent as well as prevent any problems leading to disputes and Protests.
6. Promote the implementation of policies to protect the rights and interests of migrant workers, both within the national framework, as well as in the region and with the countries concerned.
7. Continue to participate in the implementation of the national policy framework for social protection and the social security system more effectively by strengthening the exchange mechanism for consultation between service users, managers and service providers, as well as those who are obliged to provide service support.
8. Continue to strengthen cooperation with development partners to support development policies and protect the employment sector.
