The National Assembly Standing Committee meets to review the nomination of Mr. Prach Chan as the candidate for NEC Chairman before the Plenary Session
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of June 22, 2021, the Standing Committee of the National Assembly of Cambodia will hold a meeting to review the proposal to select Mr. Prach Chan as the candidate for NEC Chairman before the Plenary Meeting. Trust in the future.
The meeting was videotaped online under the chairmanship of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, with the participation of members of the National Assembly Standing Committee and the Secretary General of the National Assembly.
The agenda for this morning's meeting includes:
1. Examine the application for the election of Mr. Prach Chan as the candidate for the Chairman of the National Election Committee.
2: Examining the request for recognition of Mr. Men Kuon as the Member of Parliament for Tbong Khmum Province in place of Mr. Prach Chan who resigned.
3. Reviewing the draft report on the work activities of the National Assembly between the 5th and 6th sessions of the 6th legislature.
And 4: Examine the composition of the three secretaries of the 6th session of the National Assembly of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly.
Mr. Prach Chan was one of two candidates chosen by the winning party for the National Assembly to vote for the NEC chairman, replacing Mr. Sik Bun Hok, who resigned. In this application, there are two candidates, Mr. Prach Chan and Mr. Kar Lean.
Preparations for the election of a new NEC Chairman took place after Mr. Sik Bun Hok, Chairman of the National Election Committee, resigned on June 1, 2021, due to health problems, Mr. Sik Bun Hok was The National Assembly elected its chairman (NEC) in 2015 after a political stalemate in Cambodia after the 2013 election.
