Three Mother Nature activists, Sun Ratha and Yim Leang Hee, have been charged with insulting the King and conspiracy. Separately, Mr. Ly Chandaravuth was charged with conspiracy.
The detention order was issued by Mr. Im Vannak, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The three Mother Nature activists were arrested on June 16, 2021.
Lt. Gen. Chhay Kim Khoeun, Deputy Commissioner General and Spokesman of the National Police, confirmed that according to the case file and other evidence, the group acted with a clear organization with foreigners as map makers. To act and operate.
The arrest came after authorities investigated and found three pieces of evidence:
1: This group is an illegal organization and is backed by a foreigner named Alex.
2. All their activities are to take the name and take refuge under the label of the environment, but in order to deceive the activities to collect information on various issues related to the environment as an excuse or incitement to the public in order to oppose and overthrow the government.
3. This group operates on the basis of external financing involving terrorist financing provided by their bosses by foreigners.
He claimed that the group's activities in the past were all planned and pointed out by their foreign bosses.
Please be informed that Mother Nature Organization, which is headquartered at Wat Chamkar Chhouk, Po Meas Village, Trapeang Cho Commune, Oral District, Kampong Speu Province, established and led by Mr. Alex, was canceled by the Ministry of Interior on September 15, 2017. From expelling Alex from Cambodia.
Cambodian Embassy: Laos continues to block Vientiane for two more weeks (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Embassy in the Lao People's Democratic Republic has announced that the Lao government will continue to blockade Vientiane for another 14 days. June 20 to July 4, 2021, after 19 cases of Kovid in the community.
In this situation, the Cambodian Ambassador to Laos has informed all Cambodian citizens, workers and students who are living, doing business, working and studying in Laos to be careful and implement the health measures set by the Lao government.
The embassy also stated that in continuing to blockade Vientiane for another 14 days, the Lao government has continued to ease some measures as follows:
1: Continue to close places to eat, drink, casinos, karaoke, entertainment, massage places, sports centers of all kinds, do not sell alcohol, do not gather more than 50 people, do not allow people who have not been vaccinated Kovid-19 to travel by car and plane and ban - Enter the red zone.
2. Permission to open commercial, supermarkets, wholesale and retail markets, gyms, fishing boats, restaurants, food, cafes (seating), tourist resorts and beauty salons.
3. Allow meetings to open schools in non-communicable areas in the community. Access to and from non-Red Zone areas.
4: Can travel across the province by car for those who have already received two doses of Kovid-19 vaccine. Trucks do not need to be parked and driven into and out of the city.
