The case of two dead buffaloes running into a dead car in Peam Ro district, Prey Veng province has not been resolved yet, the case must be sent to court to continue the procedure
(Prey Veng): On June 21, 2021, for more than a week, a herd of buffaloes ran into a fish truck, causing two deaths at the scene in Prey Kandeang village, Prey Kandeang commune. In Peam Ro district, Prey Veng province, the authorities have not yet allowed the car owner to take the car away, saying it will be kept for legal settlement.
The owner of a fish truck, which contained 8 tons of fish at the time of the accident, was not immediately transferred to other vehicles, resulting in the death of more than 5 tons of fish. The buffalo owner maintained his position to claim 3 million riel in compensation, while the first incident claimed up to $ 5,000.
This case has not been resolved at the Office of Road Traffic Police of Prey Veng Provincial Police and the case has been sent to the Prey Veng Provincial Court to be resolved after the two sides failed to reach an agreement.
Deputy Commissioner in charge of the Land Traffic Office of Prey Veng Provincial Police, Mr. Ou Polin, told Fresh News on the afternoon of June 21, 2021 that the authorities still keep the same means because both parties do not. Still agreed. The case was sent to court a few days ago.
He added that the case is out of the hands of the competent authorities because it has been sent to the Prey Veng Provincial Court, so the decision to allow the car to return to the owner is at the discretion of the court, not the decision of the police. He added that in the complaint, the owner of the buffalo sued for compensation of 1.2 million riel from the car.
However, the owner of the car also expressed dissatisfaction around this case, taking the position that the car is not wrong, because at the time of the incident, the buffalo shocked his car that was driving on the road. Why did the buffalo owner come to sue and demand that you pay back the compensation?
The car owner also asked the authorities to speed up the procedure to resolve this case because it did not affect human life. He said that keeping his car for such a long time made him lose money in business.
The buffalo owner is now suing for $ 5,000 from the car company. With tons of fish in the truck, the owner asked to transfer the fish to another truck, but was not immediately authorized.
Until 8 pm on the same day, fearing to damage the fish, the car owner decided to set aside $ 2,000 to remove the car, but was not allowed to do so, causing about 5-6 tons of fish on the car died and damaged. Tens of thousands of dollars due to the delay in transferring to another car.
The owner of the fish truck expressed frustration with the local authorities' decision not to allow him to transfer the goods to another truck immediately, causing damage and no one was responsible while his truck was driving on the road. And a herd of buffalo ran in in amazement.
