(Phnom Penh): The project to build a CDC pumping station on the Tonle Sap River in Srah Chak commune, Daun Penh district, which is a grant from Japan, has been completed 95% and is scheduled to be completed in August 2021. Release rainwater from the area north of Wat Phnom and east of Monivong Blvd to Chroy Changva Bridge.
Mr. Sam Piseth added that the construction of the CDC pumping station started in June 2019, reached 95 percent and is scheduled to be completed in August 2021. He said that this station can pump rainwater from the area north of Wat Phnom and Monivong Boulevard to the Chroy Changva bridge.
The CDC pumping station is also a pumping station under the fourth phase of the Flood Protection and Drainage Improvement Project of the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) in Japan.
It should be noted that the flood protection and improvement project of the fourth phase of drainage system in Phnom Penh was opened on March 4, 2019 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The fourth phase of the Jaika Flood Protection and Drainage Improvement Project in Phnom Penh, worth a total of $ 36 million, is a grant from the Government of Japan, which includes the construction of an underground water reservoir and a pumping station. The automatic mechanical garbage truck is equipped with a water pump.
