On the morning of June 20, 2021, the Ministry of National Defense celebrated the commemoration of the struggle of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his comrades towards the national rescue and the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot on June 20. 1977 in Tonlong village, Koh Thmor commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province. The ceremony was presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh and Lieutenant General Fan Van Zhang, Minister of Defense of Vietnam.
At 9 pm on June 20, 1977, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, then known as "Comrade Hun Sen" and four loyal warriors, including Mr. Nuch Thorn, Mr. Nhek Horn, Mr. San Sanh and Mr. Va Po Ian, decided to Leaving Cambodia for Vietnam to seek support and build up an army to overthrow Pol Pot's Democratic Kampuchea regime, the most brutal regime in Cambodian history.
The escape of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his comrades is considered to be an invaluable struggle in the historical event for the nation and the people of Cambodia. To commemorate the merits and heroism of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in this National and People's Liberation Event, the Ministry of National Defense has always held a memorial service every year since 2017.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh emphasized in the ceremony this morning that the organization of this ceremony was solemn, but due to the epidemic of Kovid 19 disease, the number of participants was limited. According to Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh, despite the restrictions on such participants, some officials did not attend the invitation under the pretext of duty.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh expressed his displeasure to the officials who did not attend the invitation.
It is noteworthy that Samdech Pich Sena complained about the non-participation in this valuable event for the history of Cambodia, not only in 2021, but in 2020, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh also complained about the non-participation of officials at this invitation. .
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh expressed his determination that no matter what the obstacles or difficulties, he will organize this program every year to inform the Cambodian people about the background of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's struggle for national liberation. And the Cambodian people out of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
