Om Chhorn alias Chhom Chhorn, a 58-year-old man, was charged by Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court with "premeditated murder" in the case of shooting and killing 3 people, Bin Hoeun, who died on the spot. Occurred in front of a handicraft house producing pure water, Trapeang Chrey village, Khlong Popok commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province on May 16, 2018.
At the hearing of this case, the Criminal Judgment No. 100 "D" of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court sentenced him to life imprisonment. However, the convict, Om Chhorn alias Chhom Chhorn, appealed the decision to the Court of Appeal.
Mr. Plang Samnang, Spokesperson of the Court of Appeal, confirmed to Fresh News that on June 08, 2021, the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal brought the case of the shooting death of Teuk Soth boss in Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province to a formal hearing. In particular, despite the trial, the situation of Kovid 19 has not yet improved.
The spokesman confirmed that after the hearing, the Court of Appeal upheld the decision to announce the verdict on June 21, 2021.
