The escape of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and his comrades is considered to be an invaluable struggle in the historical event for the nation and the people of Cambodia. Because of this, the Royal Government of Cambodia, through the Ministry of National Defense, has decided to compile documents as well as all constructions at the location of the road to the national liberation struggle as a memory for all generations of Cambodians.
Construction is a reminder and remembrance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's struggle not only on Cambodian soil. In Vietnam, a number of buildings have been erected to commemorate this historic event.
On Vietnamese soil, the Vietnamese side helped build a road on the road that Samdech Techo traveled from the Cambodian border at the main road to Lok Ninh district, Song Be province, Vietnam. Vietnam also helped build a plaque on Vietnamese border. The large plaque inscribed the Cambodian and Vietnamese flags, as well as the Cambodian and Vietnamese inscriptions at the same time.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh in front of his counterpart, Lieutenant General Fan Van Zhang, called the presence of a plaque a success that Cambodia wants to preserve as a historical legacy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's national liberation struggle. Sen and warriors.
Samdech Picheay Sena emphasized, "The most important thing that I have mentioned in the series is the construction of the road from X16 to Lok Ninh district of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam." "Today we have seen a great achievement. More importantly, an inscription that we need to display as soon as possible, so in a short time this inscription was inaugurated today."
In addition to the achievements that have been showing the pagoda and inaugurated on June 20, 2021, the 44th anniversary of Samdech Techo's struggle, this morning, the Minister of Defense of Cambodia and Vietnam also invited Together, they laid the foundation stone for the construction of another Cambodian-Vietnamese friendship building, with the support of the Vietnamese side.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh also emphasized that Samdech will urge the content team to continue their efforts to further research and find historical points in both Cambodia and Vietnam in order to collect documents, equipment, weapons, preserved as strong evidence. In addition, for the youth and the next generation to have a clear and accurate understanding of the true history that evolves according to each stage that Cambodia and Vietnam went through.
