Iran and six other powers have been meeting since April to hold talks between the United States and Iran. The United States, under former President Donald Trump, withdrew from the 2015 Iran nuclear deal in 2018, accusing it of failing to comply.
Sunday's official meeting comes just one day after Ibrahim Raisi was elected the new president of Iran in Friday's general election.
The parties to the current Iran nuclear deal are Iran, Russia, China, France, the United Kingdom, Germany and the European Union. Since the US withdrawal, Iran has stepped up uranium enrichment, raising concerns that such actions could pave the way for Iran to develop a nuclear bomb.
