Mr. HUN Many: The Road to National Salvation of Samdech Techo HUN SEN on June 20, 1977, a Movement for Resurrection
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, on June 19, 2021, stated that the journey towards the national salvation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen on June 20, 1977 is a resistance movement provided. Return to survival again.
"The beginning of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's journey to national liberation on June 20, 1977 was the beginning of a resistance movement, combined with other resistance movements to overthrow the Khmer Rouge and end genocide, torture and execution. "Slavery and the return of the people to a new life, a dignified life and a long quest for peace." This is according to Mr. Hun Many confirmed on Facebook.
According to Mr. Hun Many, due to his high dedication and intelligence in handling the situation, both inside and outside the country, the dangerous and almost hopeless mission from the beginning turned into the national liberation movement that led The formation of the United Front for the National Salvation of Cambodia on December 2, 1978, which led to the glorious victory on January 7, 1979.
It was not until June 20, 1977, that the Cambodian journey began to spin in a dynamic pace and in a bright path to national unity, national unity, territorial transformation, turning Cambodia from a pile of ashes and desolation towards an island of peace, progress and prosperity. From day to day. Everything we see and live in today is the result of the decisions and clear vision of the Cambodian leaders who are at the helm of our ship today.
"Peace is indeed a precious treasure, not just to the leaders and warriors of the past," he said. "But it will be valuable for all of us and the next generation of Cambodians."
Maintaining peace is the highest duty and responsibility of every Cambodian child to ensure that the future of Cambodia will not allow the tragedy of the past to come and threaten the peace we have now. At any cost.
