The remarks of the newly-appointed Singaporean Ambassador were made during a meeting with Minister of Tourism Thong Khon on June 17, 2021 at the Ministry of Tourism.
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon spoke about the progress of tourism cooperation between Cambodia and Singapore, which led to an increase in tourism to both countries before the outbreak of Kovid-19. However, due to the global crisis, the growth of international tourism in Cambodia has slowed.
The Minister continued that the Royal Government of Cambodia has approved the launch of the "Roadmap on the Plan for the Restoration and Promotion of Cambodia's Tourism in and After the Kovid-19 Crisis" to serve as a compass for the restoration and promotion of Cambodia's national tourism. It also needs the cooperation of partner countries, including Singapore.
Upon realizing this, Ms. Tu Lechheng expressed her strong support and appreciation for this cooperation, stating that "the Government of the Republic of Singapore as well as the Embassy of Singapore in Cambodia continue to support cooperation with the Royal Government of Cambodia. "Like the Ministry of Tourism in implementing the plan to restore Cambodia's tourism sector and continue to cooperate with other Cambodian friends."
"Once the Kovid-19 crisis is eased, we will increase cooperation and mutual assistance, especially in the field of human resource training and the opening up of tourism to the two countries," she said. According to the safety rules of the Ministry of Health of both countries.
In addition, the Republic of Singapore fully supports Cambodia in preparing to host the "ASEAN Tourism Forum 2022" and the "2023 SEA Games".
Ms. Tu Le Chheng requested to cooperate with the Ministry of Tourism of Cambodia to organize tourism events or tourism exhibition events at any convenient time in accordance with the safety rules of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry of Health in order to contribute to the restoration and promotion of tourism in both countries. Two re.
