(Phnom Penh): Based on the vision of taking responsibility for the environment, Khmer Breweries has reduced the amount of water used to produce Cambodian beer per liter from 4.5 liters in 2013 to only 2.63 liters in 2020. In order to save natural resources and implement sustainable strategies.
Khmer Breweries has invested in machines and devices to measure water consumption in order to monitor daily water consumption and to identify steps or stages that use high water consumption to reduce and save money by establishing standards for use, including Employees' understanding of the cost and savings of water use.
According to the technicians of Khmer Breweries, the technology involved in saving natural resources does not affect the capacity of the beer in each can or bottle, i.e. it only creates a more efficient production line using less water.
It should be noted that the wastewater used in Khmer Breweries is passed through a liquid waste cleaning system to be cleaned before being discharged to the environment that can be reused.
