The 8th ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting-Plus demonstrates commitment to ensuring regional unity and prosperity
(Phnom Penh): In exchanging views on the regional and international security environment at the 8th ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting-Plus, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, said that today's meeting demonstrates the commitment It is our heart and soul to ensure the unity and prosperity of our region, as stated in our motto: "We care, we are ready, we are prosperous."
The 8th ASEAN Defense Ministers' Meeting (ADMM-Plus) was videotaped on 16 June 2021, hosted by Brunei Darussalam. The meeting was attended by the Ministers of Defense of the 10 ASEAN countries and the Ministers of Defense of eight other countries, including Australia, China, Japan, the Republic of Korea, India, Russia, the United States and New Zealand.
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh also shared some important security challenges in some areas, in which Samdech Pichey Sena considered Kovid 19 as one of the major challenges in the world.
"Although we have been successful in developing 19 vaccines against Kovid, we are still concerned about the new strains of the virus that are spreading around the world and the effectiveness of these new viruses," he said. "In this context, it requires joint efforts and commitment to fight this deadly epidemic."
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh further stated that in this difficult situation, the Armed Forces play an important role in solving the problem. "It is important for ASEAN military forces to work together in the fight against epidemics, as it is a cross-border security challenge that requires a joint response," he said.
On that occasion, Samdech Pich Sena thanked China, Australia for providing financial assistance and vaccines to save the lives of Cambodians.
In exchanging views on the regional and international security environment at the ASEAN-Plus Defense Ministers' Meeting, on that occasion, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh shared on other important security challenges such as maritime security, terrorism and Raise responses to regional and international security challenges through the establishment of various forums and cooperation mechanisms.
On that occasion, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh also participated in the approval of the Declaration of the Free Baghdad by the ASEAN Defense Ministers-Plus in celebration of the 15th anniversary of the ASEAN Defense Ministers towards the readiness for the future of peace and prosperity in ASEAN. Also.
