(Phnom Penh): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, congratulated the 30th anniversary of ASEAN-China Dialogue, calling it a great opportunity to enhance ASEAN-China relations. To the next high level to build a community with a common future, opening a new page towards common prosperity for ASEAN-China.
This statement was made by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh during the ASEAN-China Informal Meeting of Defense Ministers, which was videotaped on June 15, 2021, hosted by Brunei Darussalam.
"Over the past three decades, we have seen ASEAN-China relations grow closer and stronger, and China has played an important role in maintaining peace, stability, prosperity and sustainability in the region," he said. "China is committed to building trust and strengthening ties with ASEAN, especially in the field of maritime security." This is according to the additional confirmation of Samdech Pichey Sena.
He praised the success of the ASEAN-China Naval Exercise in August 2018, which strengthened naval interoperability and, more importantly, to build trust and confidence in working together to resolve maritime incidents. .
"This year marks the 30th anniversary of ASEAN-China relations, so 30 years ago, ASEAN and China built relations when the Cold War ended, especially when the world," he said. Has become multi-polar as well as economic cooperation. "Speaking of security cooperation between the two countries is to build an ASEAN-China community with a common future, it is our most important goal."
It should be noted that during the opening ceremony of the Informal Meeting of ASEAN-China Defense Ministers, the Deputy Minister of Defense of Brunei Darussalam also celebrated the 30th anniversary of ASEAN-China cooperation. He expressed confidence that ASEAN's past work with China has continued to promote mutual trust, mutual assistance and promote development and stability in the region.
The Deputy Minister of Defense of Brunei Darussalam considered the ASEAN-China Informal Meeting of Defense Ministers as one of the best dialogues, and the work will continue, especially to build mutual trust.
