(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport and Permanent Vice Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee (NRCC), chaired a meeting on June 15, 2021. Establish procedures to implement the deduction of points on driver's licenses to strengthen the enforcement of road traffic laws.
The meeting was also attended by General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner and Vice Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee, as well as ministry leaders and a number of technical officials.
The procedure for deducting driver's license points will be done through the application on the smartphone, which allows traffic police to automatically withdraw driver's license points and notify the driver's license issuers and licensees who violate the law. Road traffic.
Addressing the meeting, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol encouraged the meeting to exchange ideas and provide key inputs to improve the procedure for implementing the deduction of points on the driver's license to reach a presentation to Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Director. Minister of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the National Committee for Road Safety before deciding to go to practice.
At the same time, General Santibandit Neth Savoeun is determined to cooperate and cooperate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and technical officers to implement this initiative successfully in reducing traffic accidents and expressed his appreciation and support. Loyal to this initiative, which is a true reflection of national pride.
General Santibandit also emphasized the importance of education in all forms to all levels of the masses, especially vehicle users of all types, local educational institutions, all public and private management institutions, about the procedure for deducting points. Drive through apps on mobile.
It should also be noted that according to the Road Traffic Law, all driving licenses must have a total score of 12 points, and this number of points must be reduced according to the location of traffic offenses from 1 point to 6 points. In case of running out of points, the driver's license must be canceled. If the driver wants a new driver's license, he / she must study and re-take the driving license exam for at least 6 months from the date the driver's license is invalid.
