Read the press release below: Minister urges Sweden to encourage furniture and automakers to invest in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, requested Sweden to encourage furniture maker IKEA and automaker Volvo to seek investment opportunities in Cambodia to strengthen investment and trade cooperation between Cambodia and Sweden, as well as to help Develop Cambodia as well.
During the meeting, the Minister congratulated the Ambassador on his mission in Cambodia and thanked the Swedish Government for its active participation in cooperation in key areas, including trade. Education, capacity building of civil servants and support of the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) in Cambodia.
During the meeting, the two sides also discussed and exchanged views on promoting the multilateral trading system. In that, the Minister informed the Ambassador about Cambodia's position in adhering to the multilateral framework to solve problems in all areas in accordance with international standards and with consideration for developing and least developed countries.
The Minister requested the Ambassador to inform the leadership of the Royal Government of Sweden and the European Union of Cambodia's efforts for sustainable and equitable development in the economic, social and environmental fields.
The Cambodian side also requested to continue to facilitate and encourage key Swedish businessmen and investors, such as IKEA Furniture and Volvo, to seek business opportunities as furniture processing and parts and auto parts production are growing rapidly. Cambodia and investments in other sectors include: food processing and tropical fruits.
In response, the Ambassador noted the recent growth of the Cambodian economy and economic integration, adhering to the multilateral system, as well as the progress of regulation that serves the private sector and foreign investors in Cambodia.
The Ambassador also stressed the importance of participating in an economic development with an environment of transparency and consideration for environmental issues through the use of renewable energy. The Ambassador is confident that the Swedish Embassy in Cambodia, based in Bangkok, will continue its good cooperation with the Ministry of Commerce in order to promote Cambodia-Sweden dialogue and trade relations.
It should also be noted that the trade volume between Cambodia and Sweden in 2020 will be 64 million US dollars, while the five-month period in 2021 will be 23 million US dollars.
