In an interview with reporters, Ms. O Vandin pointed out that the planned number of vaccinations may be completed by the end of 2021 or the first quarter of 2022, while the previous plan will be completed by mid-2022. There.
Ms. O Vandin said that the reason for the speed of vaccination was faster than expected because of the number of vaccines that Cambodia ordered from China and the help of the Chinese ally. She added that the medical force, both civilian and military, is ready to inject enough people.
"I think that the 19-year-old Kovid vaccination, which the Prime Minister has put in place, will be able to reach 10 million people over the age of 18," he said. "It is possible to finish this year or at the latest by the first quarter of 2022 before the plan, because we plan to expect to reach the middle of 2022 or a little more."
In addition to the rapid pace of vaccination, O Vandin also expressed concern about the stockpiling of vaccines, which requires careful management. Finally. In the case of a large number of vaccines, but not taken care of, do not take too much.
But she emphasizes that the important thing now is that the more vaccines arrive, the better it is to use the full force as much as possible, because at present the driving force behind the vaccine is not yet fully released. She thinks that if total force can be used, the speed of vaccination will be faster.
