People in Pech Changva Commune, Baribo District, Kampong Chhnang Province Express Their Happiness After Receiving 12 Kilometers of Rubber Road from the Royal Government
(Kampong Chhnang): A 12-kilometer-long red cobblestone road in Pech Changva commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province, has been completed as a rubber road by the Ministry of Rural Development, making more than 1,000 families in Pech Changva commune happy. Everyone was happy and expressed their deep gratitude to the Royal Government and the Ministry of Rural Development for helping to build this road that is easily accessible.
Mr. Chea Vich, Chief of Pich Changva Commune, described that this road used to be a red gravel road with a lot of damage, which made it very difficult for students and students to ride bicycles or motorbikes to school. High schools in Boribo district town, as well as transporting various agricultural products from the base to the market. As for the chronically ill patient and the pregnant woman who had to give birth, she found it very difficult to travel to the hospital.
The commune chief continued that with the attention of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Ministry of Rural Development in 2018, helped build this road to turn from a red gravel road. Become a beautiful and strong paved road, which was completed in early June 2021.
On behalf of the commune authorities, representing the people in the whole commune, which has 4 villages with 1105 families equal to 4,216 people, I would like to thank the Head of the Royal Government and Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development for their help. Building the above road for the people of Pech Changva commune to travel is not as difficult as before.
