(Siem Reap): Chea Sarith, an archaeologist with the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology and Head of the Renovation Project of the Southern Library of Preah Khan, confirmed that the southern library of Preah Khan Temple was completed last month. May 2021.
In the past, the library was dilapidated and tilted to the south corner due to weak foundations and large canopy trees growing from the roof, causing large open cracks from the roof to the roof, which could face collapse.
Mr. Chea Sarith added that after the completion of the renovation of the southern library of Preah Khan Temple, the APSARA Authority plans to renovate the east gate of the Preah Iso building and repair the dam in the eastern part of Preah Khan.
