Phnom Penh Public Works Department Officials: Rehabilitation of Boeung Tumpun Canal Achieved 60% as of June 14
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Duong Chansarath, Director of the Drainage Unit of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, stated that as of June 14, 2021, the rehabilitation of Boeung Tumpun Canal is 3,710 meters long and 30 meters wide. Stung Meanchey canal to Boeung Tumpun pumping station, road 371, 60% completed, 2,200 meters long.
Mr. Duong Chansarath confirmed this on June 14, 2021 to lead the team to inspect the rehabilitation of Boeung Tumpun canal, which is nearly 4 kilometers long to drain the rain during this rainy season.
Mr. Duong Chansarath added that with the attention and guidance of Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh, in resolving the rehabilitation of the drainage system, especially the main canal in Phnom Penh, while the Department of Public Works and Transport Phnom Penh, which has a drainage unit, a pumping station and a wastewater treatment plant as implementers, has resumed activities to rehabilitate the Boeung Tumpun canal to relieve flooding during the rainy season.
Mr. Duong Chansarath continued that the rehabilitation of Boeung Tumpun canal started on April 5 and so far the team has rehabilitated 60% of Boeung Tumpun canal which is 2,200 meters long. This canal plays an important role in releasing water from Doeum Sleng canal, French canal, especially releasing water from Por Senchey, Sen Sok, Toul Kork and some parts in Chamkarmon and 7 Makara districts.
Mr. Duong Chansarath also called on the people to store garbage properly at the location designated by the garbage collection company, do not throw garbage into the canal, block the waterway can not flow to the station.
