During the meeting, Mr. Lay Sothea, Director of the Finance Office of the Provincial Hall, confirmed that in the past, there were departments and units that applied to cut the land from the state inventory to the people and government officials and the forces that occupied it. For a long time, there have been a total of eight units on state land, and now six more are applying.
Mr. Chiao Tai added that the issue of granting legal land ownership to the people is a policy of the Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, as well as relevant ministries and institutions have always been paying attention to promote implementation. Within the framework of the whole country.
In connection with the issuance of legal land or residential land titles to citizens and government officials who have been deducted from the state inventory land where they have been occupied for many years, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government, has always filed Issue guidelines based on various laws and regulations for the provincial capital to implement for them as soon as possible in accordance with the law.
The provincial governor continued, "However, the implementation of the issuance of land titles from the state inventory in accordance with the law for the people, government officials and forces in Kampot province has been complicated and protracted for a long time. Years from one provincial governor to another. Therefore, to accelerate the work to be completed quickly to avoid further challenges.
