Roles, Duties and Procedures of the Capital-Provincial Coverage-19 Commission According to the New Sub-Decree
The Capital-Provincial Kovid-19 Commission is responsible for leading operations to prevent and control the spread of Kovid-19 within the jurisdiction of each capital-provincial administration.
The Capital-Provincial Kovid-19 Commission may have as many working groups or mechanisms as may be established by the order of the Capital-Provincial Administration to serve in the fight against and control of the spread of Kovid-19.
The Commission shall carry out its work under the coordination of the Inter-Ministerial Commission and the CPPCC. Inter-ministerial committee and from the CEC.
The Capital-Provincial Kovid Disease Control Committee uses the budget of the Capital-Provincial Administration and other assistance from development partners and philanthropists and uses the seal of the Capital-Provincial Administration to carry out its work.
The Inter-Ministerial Commission for the Fight against Kovid 19 has an executive committee to guide and coordinate the day-to-day work of Kovid-19.
