(Kampong Thom): Chey Sambo Cashew Nut Handicraft, a local processing factory located in Trapeang Arak village, Chey commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, exports high quality cashew nuts to the Japanese market.
Mrs. In Lay Huot, Manager of Chey Sambo Cashew Processing Factory, said on June 13, 2021 that she was a cashew farmer with 10 years experience and was the Head of Processing Unit at Sambo Prey Kuk Cashew Processing Association. Since 2010, hand-processed cashew nuts have been delicious and have gained a good reputation and received a series of orders.
She added that this work has the following benefits:
* First: Improve the quality of fresh cashew nuts and provide high value to local farmers and farmers who have signed agricultural production contracts * Second: Ensure the production of high quality and safe cashew nuts * Third: To be the basis The foundation of promoting Cambodia's cashew nuts and reducing migration by providing employment opportunities and decent wages to women and youth in the community.
All parts of the processing industry follow the standard management system, which is the principle of the Japanese processing industry to ensure the quality and safety of cashew products for consumers. These achievements are an important part of promoting Cambodia's cashew nuts, especially in Kampong Thom, to global recognition.
Ms. In Lai Huot said that with the successful cooperation on the establishment of this pilot processing plant and the link between the public and private sector producers, her first processed cashew nuts with high quality and safety standards. Exported to the Japanese market in the amount of 10 tons, the second export, and subsequent shipments will be available every month.
At the same time, Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, urged all officials to make efforts to help people in agriculture to help boost the economy, families, people as well as the national economy.
Local people are very happy with the hope of earning extra money to support their families and reduce migration. It should be noted that Chey Sambo Cashew Nut Handicraft has 33 family members who are cultivating on 344 hectares of land and 115 employees are housewives.
