Understand Business: Tourism Entrepreneurs Reveal Rules to Keep Business Stable Despite the Kovid Crisis 19
(Phnom Penh): Two tourism experts, Mr. Din Somethearith, Founder of Phka Trakoun Village and Ms. Chhay Sivlin, President of the Cambodian Tourism Association, revealed the rules for keeping businesses afloat despite the spread of Kovid's disease 19 cases.
As tourism professionals, these two experts reveal that a long-term business depends on innovation, more creative ideas will keep the business strong. Another factor is the ingenuity to turn a crisis into a real opportunity in the context of the 19-year-old. Of course, we can not turn the 19-year-old but can turn our business around.
At the second tourism forum under the theme "Opportunities and perspectives of future tourism", Mr. Din Somethearith said that in general, on tourism, if the trend of multiple vaccines, all countries, including Cambodia are considering. How to get tourists who have been vaccinated twice?
"Speaking of business or entrepreneurship during this time, it is my strategy that all business owners should not remember (do not wait for Kovid to die or return to the original state), but all business owners should be creative on their own," he said. "Obviously, the restaurant business should stop waiting for customers to come and eat in the store, but should find a way to digitally deliver food or other goods to customers."
He added that for the hotel business, now it is necessary to expect national guests, not entirely international guests. However, if travel and meetings continue to restrict local attractions, it will remain difficult.
"From experience, I know that tourism is vulnerable, so I have to look for local guests rather than international ones," he said. "But for business owners, focusing on international visitors is a must to find a way to make the business work, because if you continue to wait a long time and not regularly."
"This is a time when we show the world that during the outbreak of Kovid 19, Cambodia has produced many unique and unique products, and this promotion has become easier through digital systems," she said. "With the posting on the Internet through various tourists, and this is a profit in advertising and free of charge."
She added that tourism operators need to know how to prepare business packages to meet the needs of local tourists and in line with the circumstances of the context of Kovid 19. And this is a time to increase knowledge, do and learn and choose a variety of methods to meet the needs of their company.
"This is also a time to digitally digitize and learn to develop this technology to do other things and be prepared to develop new tasks," she said.
