(Phnom Penh): A spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia on June 12, 2021, issued a statement clarifying that the US Embassy's accusation that "the Cambodian military did not provide full support for its visit" in review Looking at the Ream naval base is an attempt to create new problems and distort the facts, leading to further strain on military relations between the two countries.
The statement came after the US Embassy issued a statement on social media stating that Cambodia does not allow US military access to all areas. "During the brief visit, Cambodian military officials did not allow the military attaché to visit anywhere inside the naval base," the embassy said.
"Based on all of the above, the Department of Defense considers the reaction of the US Embassy to be an attempt to create new problems and distort the facts, leading to further tarnish of military relations between the two countries. The Ministry of National Defense considers the actions of the visit coordination team to be fair and professional. This is clearly stated in the statement of the Ministry of National Defense.
