This QR Code system records a unique phone number without collecting personal data or user routes. The introduction of the QR Code aims to protect the health of the people in the event of a global epidemic, as stated in Article 72 of the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Article 12 of the International Covenant on Economic, Social and Cultural Rights (ICESCR). Both laws and regulations come into force.
The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has sufficient capacity to develop and manage this QR Code system in accordance with international technical standards. In fact, ministries, institutions, embassies, companies, national and international organizations, and site owners have encouraged their citizens and staff to use the system to work with the government to protect their personal safety, public welfare, and prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
