Ms. Thak Lany was pardoned by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State of Cambodia, on March 3, 2021. The court sentenced her to prison in connection with the accusation that Samdech Techo Hun Sen was the killer of Dr. Kem Ley. Since the case, Thaksin has been on the run.
Ms. Thak Lany was sentenced by the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to 1 year and 6 months imprisonment and fined 8 million Riels and to pay 100 Riels to Samdech Techo Prime Minister on November 17, 2016 on charges On charges of public defamation and incitement to commit acts that cause serious disturbance to social security. The Court of Appeal and the Supreme Court later upheld the verdict.
The allegations came after Ms. Thak Lany in a public forum in Patang village, Patang commune, Lumphat district, Ratanakkiri province, on July 29, 2016, accusing Samdech Techo of killing Dr. Kem Ley.
In order to seek justice and purity as the supreme leader of the country, the Prime Minister, through his lawyer Kitech, filed a lawsuit against Thaksin Shinawatra, requesting that the court take legal action and demand compensation of only 100 riels. .
After being pardoned on May 14, 2021, Thaksin Shinawatra returned from Cambodia to Cambodia, and today the King issued a Royal Decree appointing her as Secretary of State for the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations. And inspection. Cambodian youths express pride and happiness with the Royal Government for the success of the gold mining business for the first time
(Phnom Penh): After the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces the success of Cambodia's first gold mining business in 2021, Cambodian youths express their pride and joy with the Royal Government and the people. Cambodians, believing that gold mining will help increase national income.
Speaking to Fresh News, Mr. Keo Serey Sambath, a law student at the Royal University of Law and Economics, said that after hearing the news of the opening of the gold mine, he was very proud and happy. Strongly with the Royal Government.
Mr. Keo Serey Sambath stated, "Personally, after hearing about the opening of the first industrial gold mine in O'Khvav, Keo Seima District, Mondulkiri Province, I am very proud and happy. With the Royal Government.
Mr. Keo Serey Sambath continued, "This gold mining business will be a source of income to support the economy and accelerate development in Cambodia in the future." On the other hand, this business may help increase employment opportunities for local people.
Nal Ramon, a student at Phnom Penh International University, said: "I am happy to see this achievement because we are able to make our own gold."
Mr. Nal Ramon emphasized that this achievement will help Cambodia to increase national income, especially it will make Cambodia more known because of the gold trade of Cambodia.
Related to the gold mining business in Cambodia, Ms. Eng Sakna, a student of the Institute of Electricity of Cambodia, said that looking at a few years ago, the mining sector in Cambodia does not seem to develop.
Ms. Eng Sakna said that most of the mining is done in the form of a family business that can only provide daily income to the people, while the large-scale mining industry is non-existent.
Ms. Eng Sakna said, "As a young Cambodian woman, I am very pleased to receive a new achievement, the gold mining industry in Mondulkiri, which will be launched from June 21 onwards. "
Mr. Chim Vichheka stated, "As a Cambodian citizen, I am very pleased with the loyalty of the head of the Royal Government under the noble leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for announcing the first victory on "Gold mining."
On the night of June 10, 2021, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, announced the first success of the gold mining business, which can produce about 3 tons of pure gold per year.
The operation of this gold mine business and gold refinery will start from June 21, 2021, located in O'Khvav area, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the gold mines that the company operates will provide an average gross income of about $ 185 million per year, of which the national budget revenue from royalties and other taxes averages about $ 40 million. One year. These funds will be used in the national budget for economic and social development.
Environmental spokesperson: Steps in the carbon credit market underscore Cambodia's improved protection of natural areas
(Preah Vihear): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Environment, confirmed that the step into the voluntary carbon credit market and further study is to confirm the improvement of the protection of natural areas. Cambodia.
