The senior official said that the Ministry of Environment, which has jurisdiction over the management of 7.3 million hectares of natural resources in more than 70 protected areas in Cambodia, has made efforts to strengthen forest protection strategies. By strengthening the capacity of park rangers, community involvement, and strengthening partnerships with partner organizations to achieve effective natural resource protection and conservation.
