Handicraft processing at Chep Wildlife Sanctuary helps improve the livelihoods of local people and raise awareness of the value of forests
(Preah Vihear): By processing handicrafts from non-timber forest products as materials and souvenirs of the community can make them earn extra income to support the family life of the people in Preah Vihear province to acquire original processing skills Resistant to become a daily use product.
Residents of Sangke village, Sangke commune, Chhep district, Preah Vihear province, in this Chhep community, take advantage of the trees by making chopsticks, swords, crutches, forks, mats, bows, and selling them on the market to become a business other than farming. .
By benefiting from this resistance, the people living in the natural resource protection area have become more aware of the importance of the forest, because after having a real livelihood and the value of Cambodia's natural resources. Made them not migrate to earn a living.
Involved in the story of the tree, as well as handicrafts processing materials from this tree, Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated, "I would like to thank the people who planted more trees for reproduction in the village. "Their area is in addition to what is already in the forest."
Standing to sell materials made from trees, Ms. Hoeun La said that since her family knows how to process trees into materials, life has become better. She can earn enough to support her family.
Separately, Ms. Tith Sokhon, a resident of Sangke village, Sangke commune, Chhep district, Preah Vihear province, said that the benefits of this tree can be used to cook a lot of leaves, roofing mats and it can be processed into many materials. Very now.
Producers of recycled materials from a tree in Chhep district, Preah Vihear province, Mr. Meas Hoeur, the head of the community of wood processing community in Chhep district, said that through the processing of materials from the tree is the people. People in the community can earn 500,000 to 600,000 riels per month. This income can make them just make a living and do not have to go to the forest to cut down trees or hunt animals like before.
It should be noted that the tree is a kind of brown plant with black stems that are 6 to 25 meters high. Its stems are long and large, so they can be processed, split into leaves, and can be used as chopsticks, as well as good quality and black when used daily.
According to research documents, the tree has flowers only once in a lifetime, it will die after its flowers ripen. In Cambodia, the tree can be found growing in some provinces such as: Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Ratanakkiri, Kratie and so on.
