Dr. Kin Phea: Vietnam should not take the issue of its immigrants to add weight to the suffering of the Cambodian people
(Phnom Penh): On June 2, 2021, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration issued a notification requiring the immediate dismantling or relocation of fish farms, floating houses, small boat houses and unregulated structures on the river surface. In Phnom Penh, leave for 1 week.
The same notice also states that if this period expires, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will take administrative action without taking any responsibility for any damage or loss. In case of stubbornness, local authorities and professional officials will build a case to be sent to court legally.
The actions of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration have received widespread support from Cambodians of all walks of life and all political affiliations. At the same time, the Cambodian people urge the Phnom Penh authorities to implement the strictest and most effective measures by not allowing illegal anarchic settlements along the river in the geography of Phnom Penh, which is the heart of Cambodia. That no.
To make matters worse, the water used by the leaders and the people of Phnom Penh is the water that the illegally settlers along the rivers defecate every day.
But what amazed and amazed all Cambodians was the rhetoric of the outgoing Vietnamese ambassador to Cambodia, Vu Quang Minh, who reacted to the Phnom Penh administration's measures.
On June 4, 2021, through his Facebook page, Mr. Wu Quang Minh claimed that the action of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, which restricts the seven days for the people who own fish, floating houses, small boats and Irregular structures on the river surface leave the water surface in Phnom Penh for a week, leaving those structures leaving the water surface is too fast and impractical.
Mr. Vu Quang Minh and the President of the Vietnamese Association in Cambodia visited the settlers along the river to be evacuated. Voice of Vietnam and Channel 4 Vietnam, which also covered the event, reported that most of the survivors were of Vietnamese descent, numbering about 1,000 families.
The rhetoric of the Vietnamese ambassador raised the question of whether the Phnom Penh administration under the Hanoi government or the Phnom Penh government had reacted in this way. Cambodia is an independent and sovereign state that has exclusive rights to its internal sovereignty as well as its external sovereignty, which is not under the jurisdiction of any foreign state.
The implementation of Cambodia's internal rules or internal laws, as well as Cambodia's foreign policy, is the exclusive right of Cambodia, which no foreign state has the right to encroach on. In fact, the actions of the Phnom Penh administration are purely an internal affair of Cambodia and have nothing to do with Vietnam. The ambassador's rhetoric is a serious insult to Cambodia's independence and sovereignty.
If the ambassador recognizes that the illegal settlers along the river are Vietnamese, all he can do is arrange for their repatriation to return to Vietnam to show their dignity. Vietnam will also show respect for the values of friendship and good-neighborly cooperation between the two countries. The ambassador should not make comments that damage friendships and hurt the hearts of the Cambodian people.
At all times, in all places, and in all meetings between the leaders of Cambodia and Vietnam, at all levels, the legislature and the executive branch, as well as the Vietnamese diplomats, always ask the Cambodian authorities to provide legitimacy and facilitate the Vietnamese settlers. Housing in Cambodia. They never discussed the possibility of repatriating the migrants to live in Vietnam themselves.
In fact, in a meeting with Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs Prak Sokhon at the ASEAN-China Foreign Ministers' Special Meeting, Mr. Bui Thanh Son, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Vietnam, requested Cambodia to continue to resolve the issue of legitimacy for Vietnamese citizens and requested Let the Cambodian authorities ensure the interests and well-being of the people of Vietnamese descent as well, while Cambodia is implementing social and economic development policies.
Meanwhile, on June 8, 2021, Mr. Sim Chi, President of the Vietnam Association, said that his association had submitted a letter to the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration requesting three points: first, requesting the most appropriate delay to change the location; Two request the Phnom Penh Capital Administration to find a new location where they can raise fish and the third request a budget to help supply them with the ability to go out.
Indeed, although Cambodia is a small state with a large heart, Cambodia always respects and values friendship and cooperation with its neighbors as well as other countries in the world. Cambodia is full of humane hearts and always respects virtues. As you can see, in every capital city of Cambodia there is a Vietnamese Association, is there the same Cambodian Association in Vietnam?
Cambodia really recognizes Vietnam for helping to liberate the Cambodian people from the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime. In response, Cambodian-Vietnamese memorials were allowed to be built in almost all provincial capitals of Cambodia. Is there a similar memorial in Vietnam?
Dr. Kin Phea, President of the International Relations Institute of Cambodia, Royal Academy of Cambodia (The views expressed in this article are those of the author)
