The United Arab Emirates, along with four other countries - Albania, Brazil, Gabon and Ghana - has been selected as a non-permanent member to replace the existing non-permanent members of five countries - Estonia, Nigeria, Saint-Vincent and the Grenadines. Tunisia, and Vietnam for the upcoming 2022-2023 term.
