In the wake of the recent success of the gold mining business, well-known Cambodian businessmen and economists are proud of the Royal Government of Cambodia for providing additional new sources of revenue to boost economic growth.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath, an economist and president of the Chinese Academy of Sciences of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, said the success of the gold mining venture was good for Cambodia in boosting economic growth by increasing government revenue.
"I understand that the discovery and exploitation of gold is one of the successes of the use of Cambodia's natural resources, a favorable factor and a driving force for Cambodia's growth through revenue," he said. Of the Royal Government, which will finance through the construction of roads, schools and hospitals.
Dr. Ky Sereyvath added that the source of revenue from this gold mine in the economy is called capital income from resources, not tax revenue, which is additional revenue because we look at the national budget. There are two types of government revenue: fiscal revenue and capital revenue.
Oknha Lim Heng, Vice President of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and a well-known businessman, said that the new revenue from the gold mining business is a valuable and useful thing and a history of Cambodia, and if we produce this gold mining business. Yes, every year this is a good thing to support and maintain the financial security of the national budget.
Tycoon Lim Heng continued that the income from this natural mineral is non-tax revenue that can maintain economic stability in the long run if Cambodia continues to produce, and this non-tax revenue stabilizes the Cambodian economy. Good. Therefore, if Cambodia earns income from other natural resources, it will be able to maintain the security of the national budget.
Tycoon Lim Heng stated, "I think this is the best thing for Cambodia and a historic piece of news that Cambodian children as well as all business people celebrate." "I believe that after Cambodia acquires this gold mine, various infrastructures will be developed."
Neak Oknha Sear Rithy said that starting a gold mining business is also attractive for mining business people to look to Cambodia more and can also create a workforce that gives people more jobs to stimulate economic growth. National. The extraction of gold can show the world that Cambodia has the resources to extract gold, so new investment will also be possible.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the gold mining business of this company will provide an average gross income of about 185 million USD per year, of which the national budget revenue from royalties and other taxes is about 40 Millions of dollars a year, and these funds will be used in the national budget to develop the economy and society.
