(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of National Defense Vaccination Team plans to complete the first and second doses of Kovid 19 vaccination for nearly 1 million people in the former Red Zone in Phnom Penh on the 20th. This is June 2021. Along with the closure of vaccination operations for people in the former Red Zone in Phnom Penh, the army team also received a new order to vaccinate people in the provinces.
On June 11, 2021, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Joint Chief of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Operation Kovid 19 Vaccination, told Fresh News that the Kovid 19 vaccination in the former Red Zone In the six districts in Phnom Penh, both the first and second doses will close on June 20. In nearly two months of operation, the army has delivered 993,902 people.
General Ith Sarath also said that after the closure of operations in Phnom Penh, the army will continue to operate in the provinces in cooperation with the provincial health department. According to General Ith Sarath, the provinces where the army has been ordered to carry out the operation include Sihanoukville, Kampong Speu, Takeo, Kampong Cham and Svay Rieng.
According to the commander in charge of the vaccination operation, 1,240,412 people will be vaccinated in the five provinces, and more than 830,000 troops will be in charge of the vaccination.
According to the plan, vaccination operations in the provinces may start on June 21, after receiving more vaccines from China on June 19. The injection will be done step by step according to the number of vaccines. The first province to start is Sihanoukville.
General Ith Sarath emphasized that all troops are highly committed to the vaccination operation, no matter how difficult or tiring it is, to achieve the plan submitted by the Royal Government and to help the people avoid attacks. Of Kovid 19 virus.
"The army comes from the people, we do all the work for the people. This vaccination work is very important for our people to avoid the harassment of Kovid 19, so all the troops are very committed. We have seen that for more than a month now, our troops have been operating without a break. "Even though we are hard, we are tired, we enjoy this important operation for our nation and our people." General Ith Sarath emphasized.
"For this new operation, our army remains highly committed to the most responsible work to vaccinate the people to achieve the plan given by the Royal Government," said Ith Sarath.
In the past vaccination operations for the people, especially in the former red zone in Phnom Penh, the army team was evaluated and praised by the people for vaccinating quickly with a high sense of responsibility and good attitude with the people. Who went to get vaccinated.
Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Vaccination Commission, said that the military team has made a significant contribution to the vaccination work. She praised and appreciated the past vaccination operations.
Ms. O Vandin thanked the vaccination team from the Ministry of National Defense and all units that have worked hard and paid high attention to vaccinating the people.
With the new assignment, General Ith Sarath also requested that the vaccination team of the Ministry of National Defense continue to be responsible for the work of vaccination, proper vaccination and cooperation. Good with local authorities to ensure that vaccinations in the provinces are successful as planned.
