The World No Tobacco Day Award Ceremony was presided over by Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health and Chair of the Tobacco Products Inspection Committee, with the participation of Ms. Ly Ilan, WHO Representative in Cambodia. And leaders of the Ministry of Health, including the Deputy Governor of Kampong Cham and the Kampong Cham Provincial Health Department.
The representative of the World Health Organization in Cambodia, Ms. Ly Ilan, congratulated Cambodia and the Ministry of Health of Cambodia on receiving the 2021 World No Tobacco Day Award for their hard work and encouragement. Placed by Minister Mam Bunheng.
"Every year, the World Health Organization celebrates World No Tobacco Day, and this year Cambodia has received two of the six World Health Organization (WHO) regional awards," she said. One is for the Ministry of Health and the other for sub-national authorities, which is a huge success for Cambodia in the tobacco control work that has been done in the past.
"We know that tobacco is killing more than eight million people every day in the world, which we can prevent," she said. In Cambodia, more than 15,000 people have died as a result of direct tobacco use and secondhand smoke. But now I see that the use of tobacco and smoking in Cambodia has decreased significantly.
