Comment: US Senate approves opposition bill to curb China's development, using competition as an excuse
BEIJING, June 8 (Xinhua) - The US Senate passed a draft law on innovation and competition in the United States on June 8 to curb China's development from all angles, using innovation and competition as an excuse.
The Cold War concept and the zero sum concept of this draft law do not fit into the current era, which is surprising. It has not only distorted the original idea of innovation and competition, but also trampled on and insulted the principles of a free market, which some Americans boast.
At present, given the ongoing globalization of the economy, any attempt to put pressure on China through the enactment of these laws will undoubtedly have a serious impact on global development and growth. And will inevitably affect personal interests.
In fact, China's development goal is not to replace the United States, but to make the Chinese people live happier and better lives. China welcomes positive competition on the basis of truth and justice, but rejects competition that attacks each other with bad intentions and zero sums, and does not allow anyone to deprive anyone of its legitimate development rights and interests. No.
