Minister of Agriculture encourages all fish farms to continue to maintain, strengthen and expand production, consolidate production, find partners, network marketing
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on June 10, 2021, encouraged all fish farms to continue to work hard to strengthen and expand fish production in time for the golden opportunity. Collaborate with the Fisheries Administration, apply proper techniques, compile production clusters, find production partners, connect marketing networks.
With the full support of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia and the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), the farm decided to invest in the construction of a fish processing factory to supply the AEON market, restaurants and hotels. In the future, it plans to cooperate with World Vision in partnership with farmers to supply the processing chain.
After examining the overall aspect and feeding (feeding) activities of the farm, the Minister praised and appreciated the efforts of the farm to adopt tilapia fish farming to contribute to meet the growing needs of the local market. Ascending.
Taking this opportunity, the Minister expressed his willingness to support and encourage the farm to continue to work hard to strengthen and expand fish production in addition to the golden opportunity to come by cooperating with the Fisheries Administration to apply the correct technique, compile production clusters, find network partners Market for the supply of processed handicrafts and increase the processing of fresh fish for the local market to increase value-added and create jobs.
In this case, Minister Veng Sakhon added that the Ministry of Fisheries Administration will be waiting to provide technical and legal cooperation for the common benefit of sustainable supply as appropriate and to export in accordance with Future Japanese market standards.
Leaving the farm, Minister Veng Sakhon, accompanied by Mr. Chao Suosdey, continued to inspect the farm's fresh fish processing factory, located in Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
He added that following the Japanese technique, a fish can be processed into 14 types of goods, including fish sauce, which is also used to make cosmetics, fish gall, fish skin and bones, and even fish wash water is used to make fertilizer.
By following the standard of proper breeding techniques, the Japanese market welcomes fish processing products from this farm, in fact, the order has increased from year to year, only 5 months in the first 5 months of 2021, the farm sells fresh fish meat 7 Tons.
Regarding the production line, the Minister expressed his hope that it will be successful due to the support of the Government of Japan through the Embassy and JICA, and especially the Japanese market.
The Minister hopes and believes that in the near future, the aquaculture sector (fish farming in general and especially tilapia fish farming in particular) will grow through Compilation of production clusters, implementation of breeding techniques in accordance with market standards, requirements and implementation of contract agricultural production.
Minister Veng Sakhon added that Japanese food (fresh fish) produced in Cambodia is a new step with the confidence and full cooperation of all stakeholders, especially the Embassy of Japan and JICA hope in the future. The breeding and processing chain will double in size to meet the needs of the domestic market and lead to exports.
