(Phnom Penh): "Cambodia-China Steel Alliance" has been fruitful for more than 60 years as the People's Republic of China celebrates the 100th anniversary of the founding of the Communist Party of the Allies. Warm blessings to China.
* Cambodia-China friendship in history books
In the Chenla folklore, a biographical account of Chiv Ta Kwan, it is said that the first Chinese to arrive in Cambodia were traders living along the Mekong River. From time immemorial, Cambodia and China have maintained friendly allies and helped each other.
Since 1956, China has begun providing economic assistance to Cambodia in the form of grants, equipment, products, and infrastructure projects. Cambodia became the first country to receive non-socialist grants from China. Similarly, Cambodia supports the United Nations in accepting the People's Republic of China as a member, opposing the "two China" act.
"Cambodia and China, together against Kovid, have made it clear that the friendship and trust between the two countries is strong and inseparable." This is what Dr. O Vandin, spokeswoman for the Ministry of Health of Cambodia, said in an interview with the media.
Kovid 19 can not hinder cooperation between Cambodia and China
So far, Cambodian mangoes have become the second fresh fruit after bananas, which can be officially exported directly to China. On May 21, the first Cambodian mangoes arrived in Guangxi, China smoothly.
Dr. Chheang Vannarith, Executive Director of the Asian Vision Institute, said that the decision to export to China and help develop the Cambodian mango industry, increase income for Cambodian farmers, it shows the importance during the economic crisis caused by. Kovid status 19.
"This is a necessary step for China to help revive Cambodia's economy after Kovid," he said. Agriculture and agro-processing are the most important sectors to improve the living standards of the Cambodian people. We hope that more Chinese enterprises will come to Cambodia to invest in related fields. ”
Over the past 63 years, Cambodia-China cooperation and many achievements have been presented in all forms. We have two languages but one heart. From the leadership to the people of the two countries, the spirit of steel friendship continues.
* Leaders' views on Cambodia-China alliance
China has provided us with a lot of help, generously, unconditionally and in all its forms, making us historically successful. I, Your Majesty, believe that going forward, China will still be the most important supporter for our country! The words of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk thank China when he left in 1975.
We are extremely proud to be acquainted with Chinese leaders of all terms and to have a special relationship with each other. Preah Sihanouk's Queen Sovanny during her visit to China in 2019.
In 1964, when receiving a delegation from the National Assembly of Cambodia, Mr. Zhou Enlai, Prime Minister of the People's Republic of China, said: "The Chinese people would like to extend a special welcome to all of you who have come this time. Because under the direct leadership of His Majesty the King, the independence progressed remarkably. We are all good friends already and now we are even closer.
* Cambodian people's view of China
In the joint fight against Kovid 19 between Cambodia and China, there are many emotional aspects.
On the morning of February 5, 2021, 5021 love masses donated by the families of Cambodian children who are recovering from congenital heart disease, a total of 86 families were sent to Khun Minh, Thailand.
A mother of a Cambodian child said angrily: "Doctors from Yunnan have rescued my children. I hope these masks can help them get through this difficult time." This cross-border love connection shows the sincere feelings of the two nations.
* In a survey of Cambodian people's perceptions
In terms of infrastructure, economy and public services, 44% of the speakers were China, 38% were Japan, followed by the United States (25%).
* Chinese people's view of Cambodia
"Cambodia is also my second hometown!" These are the words of Huang, a Chinese man who has struggled in Cambodia for many years. In 1996, he was full of entrepreneurial will towards Cambodia, invested and opened a factory for 20 years now.
"My children can not only speak Chinese but also speak Khmer," he said. "Over the past 20 years, he and his family have been rooted in Cambodia, adapting to Cambodian life. The struggle of the Cambodian people.
Through the close economic and trade ties between Cambodia and China, more and more Chinese people have adapted to Cambodian society. The Chinese in Cambodia highly valued the friendship between the two countries and wished the Cambodia-China friendship to last.
A sister who owns a Chinese restaurant in Phnom Penh said that she has been in Cambodia for more than 20 years and the name "Beijing Restaurant" comes from the King and Queen of Cambodia. Every year, he goes on vacation to Beijing, and the name Beijing is well known to Cambodians. Since opening the shop, it has been very popular among Cambodians in the area.
Mr. Ou, who is currently a teacher in Cambodia, said: “I have been teaching Chinese in Cambodia for more than two years. The international school I am teaching has been cooperating with a university in China for 5 years and I myself recently graduated to work in Phnom Penh. The kids here love learning Chinese.
Kao, the owner of the Northeast restaurant, said: “Two years ago, in response to the One Belt One Road policy, I came to Cambodia to participate in the development of the food sector. In the last two years, I have observed that Cambodia has changed a lot, more and more Cambodians can speak Chinese.
A military plane carrying 14 people crashed near Myanmar's second most populous city, Mandalay, on Thursday morning, killing 12 people. This was released by the Xinhua News Agency on Thursday afternoon, June 10, 2021.
A plane crash in the central part of the country has killed at least 12 people and injured two others who were taken to a nearby military hospital, according to the Mandalay Fire Department.
