(Preah Vihear): The 2021 Vulture Census in Cambodia, co-organized by the Ministry of Environment and partner organizations in the field of natural resource conservation, was launched on June 9, 2021 at four locations in the protected area in Geography of Preah Vihear, Mondulkiri, Stung Treng and Ratanakkiri provinces, where vultures are believed to be present.
This is a biodiversity monitoring survey in a protected area in Cambodia to find out what biodiversity wildlife is present in the protected area to facilitate the preparation of a highly effective protection and conservation plan aimed at maintaining The biodiversity that Cambodia has.
Preliminary results of the vulture census in the same Chep Wildlife Sanctuary on June 9 will be finalized on the evening of June 9. It should be noted that at the vulture restaurant in Dang Plit village in Chep Wildlife Sanctuary, during the monthly feeding on May 31, 2021, experts found the presence of 61 vultures, including 40 gray vultures. Two fire vultures and 19 brown vultures.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra said that the reason why vultures in Cambodia are declining is due to the greatest threat from human pollution, loss of habitat, lack of food, hunting through traps and pollution.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment called on all citizens to participate in the conservation and protection of vultures by stopping hunting or wildlife trade.
He said vultures are gentle and clean-up by eating other animal carcasses and protecting and conserving vultures. Collect value for biodiversity conservation and attract tourists for eco-tourism, create jobs, provide income for people. General Knowledge: Do you believe that "whip" is faster than sound?
