Commentary: Tourism in the old revolutionary area of the Chinese Communist Party is a good way to spread the revolutionary tradition of the Chinese Communist Party in the new era
When talking about tourism in the old revolutionary areas, you will first think of the museum commemorating the opening of the first Congress of the Communist Party of China. One hundred years ago, along with Marxist doctrine widely spread in China, to meet the needs of China's revolutionary development, some leading figures decided to form the Chinese Communist Party.
On March 16, 2021, His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, visited the Museum commemorating the opening of the First Congress of the Communist Party of China (CPC) and said that this is a place of worship. Due to its political and historical significance, it is a testament to the history that the Chinese Communist Party has overcome all difficulties to build the country and serve the people.
China's revolutionary history seems to be nutritious for educating the people. In the old revolutionary areas, tourists can reminisce about the glorious journey of the Chinese Communist Party and also feel the spirit of the heroes who passed through the ages. To promote the revolutionary tradition of the Chinese Communist Party in the new era.
