Based on the above arguments, KrisEnergy was immediately granted bankruptcy protection and was able to obtain some additional funding for the development of Cambodia's first test well to reassure creditors of its ability to recover financially. The object of the company and the possibility that the creditors may turn the debts into an investment in the company's shares.
The Secretary of State said that the current production is from 5 test wells in a small production area of the whole block A, not the whole block A. This area has a total area of about 110 square kilometers, while the entire block A has a total area of about 3,000 square kilometers.
