Mr. Sok Kim Choeun, Director of the Department of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation of Kampot Province, told Fresh News on June 9, 2021 that this year, 65,000 tons of salt production has been achieved and there are 4 stocks of salt left. Another 50,000 tons. So the salt for this year is enough to meet the demand.
"So far we have more than 65,000 tons of salt collected from production, plus 45,000 tons of salt we have left in stock for this year, our salt can "Supply to the domestic market as last year, no need to import."
He added that at the beginning of the year and at the beginning of the salt production season, the most productive producers released the salt for sale to raise capital for their production process, and then the price of salt was low. While brokers and depots have the opportunity to collect salt at the beginning of the season for storage, brokers and depots will resell it during the season when the people make prahok with higher prices than at the beginning of the season.
He added that in general, the market supply of salt is between 100,000 tons per year, and salt production is most productive during the three consecutive months of February, March and April, because these three months are hot months. Strong salt production yields a lot.
He said that the salt production process in June this year saw more weather problems than last year, with continuous rains, which caused salt production to almost be closed by 2020. Producers can continue to produce salt until August. Therefore, the rainy season in June this year may lead to the inability to continue salt production and reduce the number from last year.
