The first handover ceremony of Cambodia's oil drops at the Victory Monument was held this morning, June 9, 2021, presided over by Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense. Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Founder of Win-Win Politics, Founder of Peace in Cambodia, and many other relevant officials.
Minister Suy Sem stated that the main meanings of Cambodia's first oil droplets, which are designed in the Khmer style, are as follows:
* First: A drop of oil in the form of a lotus or Po leaf, representing prosperity, purity, growth, which is the treasure of Cambodia. The 29-centimeter-tall glass drops represent the 29th day of Cambodia's first drop of oil.
* Second: The trophy trophy represents the efforts of the leaders to achieve fruitful results, namely access to oil resources for the development of the motherland of Cambodia. The 12-cm-tall lotus trophy represents the month of December or December, receiving Cambodia's first drop of oil.
* Third: The Lion Foot Trophy and the Foot Trophy represent the support of the Cambodian people and civil servants who are the staff of the Royal Government and other relevant officials in their efforts to work to extract the benefits of natural resources to develop the society. . The 20-centimeter-tall lion's foot and foot trophy represent 2020, receiving Cambodia's first drop of oil.
* Fourth: The lamp decoration decorated with three-headed dragons symbolizes prosperity and represents the year of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the period that received the first drops of oil in Cambodia.
Minister of Mines Suy Sem added that Cambodia's first drop of oil obtained in the context of the difficult global economic situation threatened by the Kovid-19 pandemic is a testament to the Royal Government's efforts, perseverance and success. Investors we all admire, too.
Please note that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has emphasized that the amount of oil that Cambodia receives, it is a small amount, yet does not affect the economy. But it was a good start to the oil and gas industry in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Prime Minister has said that the extraction of drops of oil, although small, is a happy achievement and a source of pride for the people of Cambodia. Samdech Techo, Founder of Win-Win Politics, Founder of Peace in Cambodia, highlighted that this drop of oil is an achievement born of win-win politics.
Samdech Techo also stated that the first drop of oil in the history of Cambodia is a blessing for the people and the nation of Cambodia, not a curse as mentioned by some unscrupulous people. The revenue from the sale of Cambodia's oil will be used in two priority areas: education and health.
