Siem Reap Provincial Administration Announces Search for 19 Positive Kovid Fugitives
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration on June 8 announced the search and identification of 19 positive Kovid suspects who refused to cooperate with the authorities to take samples and escaped.
According to the press release of the Siem Reap Provincial Administration, the person named Van Veasna, 27 years old, was born in Lvea village, Kampong Russey commune, Po Rieng district, Prey Veng province.
The man was in direct contact with a Kovid 19-positive person at the Natural World restaurant. Authorities arrived at the man's temporary address at a rented room in Phum Khnar, Sangkat Chreav, Siem Reap (behind the Angkor Era Hotel), but he did not cooperate and fled.
The provincial administration calls on Mr. Van Veasna to hurry up and cooperate with the authorities and the medical team to get a sample of Kovid-19 disease test.
The provincial administration also announced to the citizens who are directly and indirectly involved with Mr. Van Veasna to hurry to do the right thing and monitor their health in case of suspicion or health changes, please provide information to 012 955 474/077 789 007 For the team to take action to take a research test sample.
