(Kampong Chhnang): They may not have forgotten the story of two veterans, a couple who grow crops near the foot of a remote mountain in Kampong Chhnang province and have the idea of a small hydropower for daily use by pulling water from On that mountain, the authorities have now informed them to move to another place after claiming that they are staying illegally.
It is unknown at this time what he will do after leaving the post. It is unknown at this time what he will do after leaving the post. Small hydropower for daily use.
Recall that this ex-military man has an admirable innovation, he was able to create a small hydropower using water flowing from the top of the mountain, the anniversary of the rainy season through water drills, 24-hour rotation, dynamo traction. 10 kW generates electricity for use in plantations and in their homes, as well as water from drills to irrigate crops in the field easily.
Mr. Phok Heang, 63 years old, living on a farm at the foot of Roleap Kuy mountain in Roleap Kuy village, Chiep commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province. It's been years since he invented it himself, and it took him months to successfully generate electricity through the small hydropower plant above.
He added that not only in the plantation, he also used more than 30 light bulbs to illuminate around the house at night, and used electric cookers, kettles, two refrigerators in the room and Computers and televisions even have easy access to welding stations.
Mr. Phok Heang stated that this water drill uses only 24 propellers, if used more, it can not rotate with the force of water flow, because in the dry season, the water falling from the mountain seems to be weaker than in the rainy season. Made both seasons required at once.
As for the use of electric water drills, he knew that it would be convenient for his family to live in the remote mountains from the villagers, which are more than 10 kilometers away, where there are not many people coming and going because But the road is difficult and there is no electricity to use.
