Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh Receives US Military Attaché to Discuss Work After Agreeing to Inspect Ream Port
(Phnom Penh): On June 7, 2021, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, allowed the outgoing US Attaché and the new US Attaché to meet at the Council of Ministers.
After the meeting, Samdech Pichey Sena confirmed to Fresh News that during the meeting, the two sides presented some relations and cooperation in the past. He praised the United States for helping to train the Cambodian military's human resources and called on the US Joint Chiefs of Staff to continue the cooperation between the Cambodian and US armies, which had failed in the past due to the Kovid-19 crisis.
The meeting between the Cambodian defense chief and the US military attaché came after Cambodia agreed to a US request that would allow the US military attaché to inspect the port of Ream in the near future to dispel any doubts about Chinese military bases.
However, in the above meeting, the two sides have not set a specific time to visit Ream.
In the past, some US media outlets have continued to attack Cambodia for allowing China to set up military bases in countries in the Ream region, while Cambodia has repeatedly stated that it does not violate the country's supreme constitution. No, there are no foreign military bases in Cambodia like the propaganda.
Regarding the case of Ream Port, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh stated that Cambodia only received assistance from China, a steel friend, to help build a larger and more modern Ream Port, and this assistance was not available. Conditions like other powers.
Samdech made it clear that the Ream port is currently under construction and after construction, Cambodia is the consumer of this modern port, without handing it over to China as alleged by the United States.
