(Phnom Penh): The first vaccination campaign in the former Red Zone in 6 districts in Phnom Penh by the Armed Forces was completed on June 7, 2021. During the 38 days of operations in the former Red Zone, nearly 1 million people were vaccinated.
On May 1, 2021, the army began vaccinating people in the former Red Zone, an area at high risk of the spread of Kovid 19, under the direct command of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen. The former Red Zone, which was vaccinated by the army, has six districts: Meanchey, Por Senchey, Dangkor, Kampoul, Toul Kork and Russey Keo, equivalent to about 43 communes.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Operation Kovid 19 Vaccination, Ministry of National Defense, told Fresh News on the night of June 8, 2021 that the first dose vaccination operation in the former Red Zone All six districts have been completely closed, while the second dose is scheduled to close in the next few days.
After receiving orders from Samdech Techo, more than 3,000 troops from various units entered the vaccination operation for the people in the former Red Zone. They are highly committed to this operation, with no holidays for the past 38 days.
As the leader of this operation, General Ith Sarath expressed his pride and admiration for his comrades who performed their duties responsibly to accomplish the work of the Royal Government and to help the people avoid harassment. Kovid's disease 19.
General Ith Sarath described the completion of the first dose of vaccination in the former Red Zone as a major achievement for the army's mission and the success of the Royal Government and the people of Phnom Penh in the fight against Kovid 19.
