(Phnom Penh): KOICA Office in Cambodia provides training to Royal Government of Cambodia officials on "Capacity Development Program for National School of Local Administration (Cambodia)." This training will be conducted online from June 8 to June 14, 2021.
The program aims to strengthen the capacity of Cambodian government local officials by sharing Korea's experience in human resource development (HRD) and human resource management (HRM) systems.
The first year of training aims to improve participants' awareness of the importance of training government officials and to develop effective action plans based on a policy analysis of Cambodia through case reports.
The second year of training is designed to strengthen the capacity of local administrators (NASLA) national trainers, including the design and development of curricula, teaching methods, and to develop action plans based on an analysis of the current situation of local schools (NASLA). ) With the case report.
The third and final session focused on advising on the implementation of the action plan, reviewing the presentation of lessons to share Korea's experience and knowledge of the management and operation of the Government Officials Training Institute and To prepare a final action plan based on the progress of the first and second years.
The program was attended by 22 participants from the Ministry of Interior, including the Department of Training, the Department of Personnel and Sub-National Administration from Ratanakiri, Pursat, Kampong Cham, Banteay Meanchey, Koh Kong, Kampong Thom and Siem Reap. Of the 22 participants, six were deputy governors from Ratanakiri, Pursat, Kampong Cham, Banteay Meanchey, Koh Kong and Kampong Thom provinces.
The Cambodian government highly values Korea's leading role in areas such as direct investment, tourism, cultural exchange, cooperation, development, vocational training, information technology, construction, finance and aviation, all of which contribute to the development process in Cambodia. The Republic of Korea is committed to these strong exchanges and cooperation to take our bilateral relations to a new level.
