China is considering passing a new law to ban military insults or defamation
BEIJING: Chinese lawmakers are considering passing a new law banning insults or defamation of military officials. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday evening, June 7, 2021.
The draft law on the protection of the status, rights and interests of military officers was submitted to the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress on Monday for review. According to the draft law, no organization or individual can insult or defame the military, and those who violate the law will face prosecution.
According to the draft law, Chinese prosecutors can prosecute or file lawsuits against insults or defamation, as well as protect the rights of the military, as well as activities that seriously impair their performance and mission. They serve the interests of society.
