(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has begun implementing hot measures at weighing stations to monitor vehicles entering and exiting. The new measure is that the ministry has embedded an underground scale in front of the weighing station and installed a camera that can record and transmit all activities and data of passing vehicles.
Overcrowding has been found to be a major cause of road damage. At this time, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has taken another step to tighten the work at weighing stations and prevent trucks from weighing.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that at this time he had decided to introduce a new measure to monitor the performance of the weighing station by installing an underground scale before entering the weighing station and equipping several cameras to capture Those car activities.
The senior minister emphasized, "I advise the officials not to joke about this. "Working on the scales, we have a clear tracking system, smart camera system (smart camera), see all the hours, the car out, the car speed, I know how much weight."
"We have taken a lot of measures to use modern technology to prevent a small number of corrupt officials," he added.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also said that the ministry has now begun piloting this measure at the Prek Eang truck weighing station. According to the senior minister, before using this measure at the Prek Eang truck weighing station, officials reported that he had only more than 200 weighing vehicles per month. But after loading, there are more than 100 vehicles weighed per day.
Mr. Sun Chanthol claimed that this measure will be implemented at all weighing stations across the country to prevent overweight shipments.
Heang Sotheayut, director of the Department of Information Technology and Public Relations and spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, told Fresh News that the new system, which the ministry has set up, has a high degree of control over the performance of weighing stations and transit truck activities. Weighing station.
According to Heang Sothea Yuth, this system can capture vehicle information, entry, weight, transportation, vehicle registration, check information and other information.
"What we do is, if we talk about the level of control, it is high because it knows the information of the vehicle," said Sothea Yut. The vehicle is properly registered, what is the owner's name, phone number, check address and related information is all the capture system.
Mr. Heang Sotheayut also pointed out that the new measures introduced by the Ministry are aimed at strengthening the work efficiency at weighing stations and to prevent overweight transport that leads to road damage. In addition, the measure is also a wake-up call for transporters to enforce shipping rules.
Currently, the Ministry of Public Works and Transport has been implementing strict measures against overweight transport. Overweight transport is in addition to the legal penalty, and for vehicles over 20 percent, the vehicle will be suspended for one year.
