(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, on the afternoon of June 6, 2021, led a delegation from Cambodia to attend the ASEAN-China Foreign Ministers' Special Meeting and Meeting. The Sixth Mekong-Lanchang Foreign Minister held on June 7 and 8, 2021 in Chongqing, China.
The invitation to attend the meeting came at the invitation of Chinese State Councilor and Foreign Minister Wang Yi. According to a Foreign Ministry statement released today by Fresh News, the ASEAN-China Foreign Ministers 'Special Meeting to be held on June 7 is part of the commemoration of the ASEAN-China Foreign Ministers' Meeting. 30th ASEAN-China Dialogue
At the meeting, the ASEAN and Chinese Foreign Ministers are expected to review the progress of specific cooperation in various fields as well as discuss further enhancement of the ASEAN Strategic Partnership. China in the current context of the Kovid-19 pandemic and emerging challenges. The ASEAN and Chinese Foreign Ministers will also exchange views on regional and international issues of common concern.
