(Kampot): During a visit to National Road No. 3 from Kampot City to Veal Renh in Prey Nob District, Sihanoukville Province, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol said that it was very embarrassing for him as the Minister of Public Works and Transport. Which was built and damaged many times.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol asked for understanding and apologized to the people for this issue.
The section of National Road No. 3 connecting Kampot City to Veal Renh, Prey Nob District, Kampot Province has a total length of more than 54 kilometers. This stretch of road has been built and upgraded many times. According to Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, this section of road was built in 2004, 2008 and 2018. But after construction, it is not used much, it is still damaged.
"As the Minister of Public Works and Transport, I would like to apologize to the road users for the inconvenience," he said.
"This is a project that I am ashamed of as the Minister of Public Works and Transport. This road is not strong," he said. "But we do not know why it is not strong."
With the apology and shame of the construction of this section of road, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol in front of the media during the inspection of the quality of the road on June 5, 2021 also presented the background of the road construction problems. And broken and measures to solve this problem as well.
According to the senior minister, six KCI construction consultants and one secretary of state at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, who manages the road project, have been removed.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol also pointed out that in the length of the road more than 54 kilometers from Kampot to Veal Renh is about 20 kilometers from Trapeang Ropov, Prek Tnaot commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province to the road junction was severely damaged. .
The 20-kilometer stretch of road damaged a 15-kilometer stretch of road due to poor foundation construction, while a 5-kilometer stretch connected to a road junction, the ground conditions were up to 18 meters deep, which is one of the main causes. Leads to road construction and is always damaged.
Mr. Sun Chanthol demonstrated the techniques that make this road strong, which was also studied by professional officials of the Ministry. According to the Senior Minister, in order for the 20-kilometer stretch of road to be strong and undamaged, the 15-kilometer-long road must be excavated, reinforced with concrete, 2.6-meter-thick concrete and widened to 12 meters.
Separately, the length of the road is about 5 km to the junction of Veal Renh, the pillars must be poured into the ground and then poured concrete on a thickness of 2.6 water and widened the road to 16 meters. The senior minister claimed that doing so would make the stretch of road paved and undamaged.
Although the study found the construction technique of this road to be strong, but the Ministry has not been able to proceed with the construction of this road because it costs a lot of money. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol.
The minister emphasized that in order to make this 20-kilometer road strong, it needs more than 60 million US dollars to build it, so now the ministry does not have the budget and is looking for funds to build. The senior minister stressed that if there is not enough funds to build technically, he will not build this road because it will be built and will face damage.
However, during this transition, the Royal Government, through the Ministry of Economy, has dropped about $ 700,000 for some improvements and repairs to make travel less difficult.
