(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) in the upcoming pilot election will establish five sample political parties, represented by each of the Capital / Provincial Election Secretariat (CEC) for registration. Candidates of political parties to stand for election in 25 target communes (twenty-five) in the provincial capital for the by-elections.
In this process, in order to facilitate the preparation of the list of candidates and to facilitate the verification of the NEC before deciding to recognize the registration of political parties, the NEC has established a "program. "Computerized Voter List" which guarantees:
For this pilot election, the preparation of the list of candidates for the election must be done in two ways:
* The first method is to prepare the list of candidates by hand (according to the old procedure), in which case, after receiving the official application for registration (T.1008), the NEC must enter the data of those candidates. Enter the computer system to verify the accuracy of the data and conditions of the candidate's candidacy to the official voter list and the documents that meet the criteria for reviewing and deciding on the application.
* The second method is to prepare the list of candidates according to the "computerized list of candidates" by the NEC, as stated above. After preparation, the political party shall keep the data of this candidate list in a flash and shall publish this list as an attachment with the application for registration (T.1008) which must be submitted directly to the NEC.
After deciding to officially recognize the list of candidates, the NEC must send the documents and the list of candidates according to the hierarchy to the NEC in accordance with the law in force.
Please note that political parties registered under the Law on Political Parties at the Ministry of Interior can participate in the training and observe the pilot election process.
