By: Puy Kea This off-screen story is not the author's opinion or analysis, but an excerpt from the discussion and excerpt from the source, compiled in short sections to make it easier for the reader to understand. And consider for yourself, because the author does not synthesize anything or content. Samdech Techo orders the construction of a health center school for veterans in Bun Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung, while Samdech Kittipritthbandit donated 80 houses
(Pursat): In order to help the veterans live in the new territory in the village of "Bun Rany Sen Chey Damnak Troyeung", the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has ordered the construction of schools and health centers on this village land.
On June 5, 2021, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Veterans Association, continued to visit and study with Mr. Mao Thanin, Governor of Pursat Province and General Kheng Someth, Commander of Samdech Techo Hun Engineering Corps. Sen.
Currently, about 80 of the more than 600 veterans' homes have been completed and are gradually being relocated.
On the area where 80 houses have been built, Mr. Mao Thanin used the army in the province to help prepare the fence of the house, clear the land, plant fruits such as mangoes, coconuts and oranges for the veterans. In addition, there is land clearing and infrastructure such as roads, toilets and digging wells.
According to Mao Thanin, each veteran's home will be equipped with solar panels to generate electricity for home use.
The provincial governor stressed that the arrangement of the houses is arranged like the houses of ordinary people in order to facilitate the living conditions of the veterans who are the benefactors of the nation. According to Mr. Mao Thanin, paying attention to the arrangement of the house and the cultivation is a high guidance and indication of Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
Although the new residence, which is a warm shelter for veterans in Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, is not yet ready, but the families of veterans have gradually moved in. With the resettlement, they began to set up houses and grow crops on the most fertile land in the agricultural sector.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, on behalf of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's staff on the work of the veterans, expressed his deep gratitude to Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit for taking care of the lives of the veterans.
Veterans, all of whom are in need and disabled, have expressed great joy and excitement when they received land to grow crops and a decent place to live. Another indescribable excitement is the direct consideration and management of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Veterans said they would remember the great merits of the two princes, and this memory will be passed on to their descendants.
