(Siem Reap): Many species of fish and birds in the Pea Conservation Area in Siem Reap province have died in recent days due to the hot weather.
Peanut Lake is a conservation area for many species of fish and birds, located in Sangkat Chreav, Siem Reap.
Mr. Soeun Sambo, Conservation Director of Peanut Lake Tourism Community, said that in recent days, hot weather and shallow water have caused the water to become very hot, which has caused many fish to die in a worrying manner. The dead fish included nearly 100 kilograms of squid, catfish and squid.
Birds, on the other hand, are sick and some even die. Veterinarians from conservation organizations and veterinarians from the Department of Agriculture are treating the sick animals.
Mr. Soeun Sambo said the community was working to save the species by hitting a large well and digging a large, deep pond, then pumping water.
It should also be noted that the Siem Reap Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has started sending machinery to Pearang Lake after the Siem Reap provincial administration agreed to the community's request, as the lake is very dry in the dry season this year. This work has been done gradually, but digging in the size of a small pond that can not save a lot of fish.
