Senior Minister Sun Chanthol inspects the almost completed section of National Road 3
(Phnom Penh): The 135-kilometer stretch of National Road No. 3 from the Chaom Chao roundabout in Phnom Penh to Kampot in southwestern Cambodia has been almost completely renovated and built.
The National Road No. 3 connecting Phnom Penh to Kampot province was inaugurated on May 7, 2018 under the high presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Director. Minister of Cambodia. As of May 2021, the construction and improvement of this road has taken 4 years, and the construction and improvement is almost complete.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, accompanied by officials of the Ministry and the construction company, on Saturday morning, June 5, 2021, inspected and evaluated the quality of construction of this road.
Road quality is an important goal and condition for Senior Minister Sun Chanthol. During the construction of this road, the Minister of Public Works and Transport always inspected both open and closed to the company to ensure that this road was built in accordance with the terms of the contract.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol told reporters while inspecting the road that National Road 3 is scheduled to be completed in September 2021.
The senior minister added that the quality of the road construction is good. However, the Ministry has not yet decided to sign the agreement, waiting for the inspection and quality mail again when the road is completed.
With the construction nearing completion, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol called for the maintenance of the road. In particular, transporters should not carry heavy loads that lead to road damage.
The Minister also urged people to use the road to respect traffic laws to avoid traffic accidents.
