(Phnom Penh): Celebrating the National and World Environment Day on June 5 under the theme: "Biodiversity and Human Health" On June 5, 2021, the Ministry of Environment announced the automatic camera recording of rare animals. Many species in the Oral Wildlife Sanctuary in Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang and Pursat provinces.
The senior official of the Ministry of Environment confirmed that the collection of data on rare wildlife species in the wildlife sanctuary now is the best news one day before Cambodia and the whole world are ready to celebrate the Environment Day in This year focuses on the restoration of ecosystems, and Cambodia focuses on the theme "Biodiversity and Human Health".
He pointed out that in this study, officials from the Ministry of Environment installed 85 automatic cameras in the Oral Wildlife Sanctuary in Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang and Pursat provinces in order to increase knowledge of study methods and biodiversity data collection. Find out the presence and absence of endangered and threatened species, as well as assess the status and distribution of important wildlife.
This project is divided into 5 components: 1: Strengthening the capacity to plan and manage landscape areas in protected areas, 2: Strengthen opportunities for the development of ecotourism and non-timber forest value chains, 3: Promoting connectivity Rural access roads, 4th: project management, monitoring and evaluation, and 5th: emergency response.
