General Vong Pisen Receives Old-New US Military Attach
(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), on the morning of June 4, 2021, paid a courtesy call on Lt. Col. Marcos Ferara, the outgoing US Joint Chiefs of Staff in Cambodia. With that, Colonel Arisree Bujio, the new Director of the United States Joint Chiefs of Staff, also paid a courtesy call and appeared on the occasion.
During the dialogue, Colonel Marcos Ferrara highlighted two important points during his tenure in Cambodia: the first outbreak of Kovid-19 and the second, the relationship between the two armies (Cambodia-US). .
In response, General Vong Pisen highlighted the diplomatic relations between Cambodia and the United States, which have existed for 71 years, which have been good ever since.
In addition, the Commander-in-Chief highlighted the US Army's cooperation in supporting the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) to conduct missions within the United Nations, including demining training. Maritime security, and more recently, funding to fight Kovid-19.
He also mentioned the good cooperation between the two armies in the search for the remains of missing American soldiers in Cambodia, as well as counter-terrorism cooperation, humanitarian work, military science research and guard exercises. Angkor and so on.
General Vong Pisen strongly believes that in the future, the relationship between the two countries' armies (Cambodia-US) will continue to cooperate well with each other.
