Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that this is an effective and sustainable mechanism for the protection and conservation of natural resources, in addition to adhering to law enforcement and cultivating a love of nature.
"This eco-tourism development investment is to create more new eco-tourism resorts that are attractive for nature lovers to explore and explore Cambodia's rich natural resources and biodiversity. "Ecotourism is also an important part of promoting education and cultivating the spirit of people to love and participate in protecting natural resources and conserving biodiversity." This is further confirmed by Mr. Net Pheaktra.
Meanwhile, Mr. Net Pheaktra said that in 2020, the eco-tourism community in the protected area received 643,000 national and international tourists to visit the eco-tourism area. At least $ 30 million will be injected into the local economy by 2020 through eco-tourism. According to the report, ecotourism communities earn between $ 50,000 and $ 180,000 per community per year.
He said that the income poured into the economy came from ticket sales, boat rentals, cruises, transportation, accommodation, souvenirs. This does not take into account the cost of food and other items that tourists spend, such as buying clothes, shoes and other items for trips and accommodation in the forest.
