At present, the body of Senior Minister Tram Iv Tek is being kept at his home near Khemma Hospital in Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh. His body will be cremated in front of Wat Botum Vat, as will other dignitaries.
Three financial associations in Cambodia jointly promote the sale of insurance products through banking institutions to the public
(Phnom Penh): The Banking Association of Cambodia, the Cambodian Microfinance Association and the Insurance Association of Cambodia have organized the first joint workshop on "The Function of Bank in Cambodia". Bankasuren is the sale of insurance products through banking institutions.
The workshop was organized to further promote the sale of insurance products through banking institutions to the public and was held after a declaration on the conditions for banking and financial institutions to conduct business in Benghazi issued by National Bank of Cambodia on March 31, 2021.
"This workshop is in accordance with the Prakas and Regulatory Framework of the National Bank of Cambodia for Banking and Financial Institutions to conduct Bankasuren business in order to improve the financial environment by increasing access to the public services," he said. "Insurance will strengthen consumer protection."
"Based on past experience with financial institutions, the reasons why some clients go bankrupt or fail include health problems, accidents, and natural disasters," he added. "To help strengthen consumer protection through insurance products and services is very important to prevent and reduce all these risks."
Huy Vatharo, President of the Insurance Association of Cambodia, said that insurance services are a risk management tool to protect the security and financial stability of individuals and businesses in the process of economic development.
"The delivery of services or insurance products to the people will significantly contribute to increasing the use of insurance services that will provide resilience," Vataro said. "Therefore, insurance operators are always looking for ways to create a distribution network for a wide range of insurance products and to provide effective services or insurance products to the people at affordable prices that they can afford."
He said that among those distribution channels, the sale of insurance products through a bank called Bank Casuren is the most widely used and efficient distribution network in various markets in the region and the world, especially for insurance. Life and micro insurance.
Mr. Kith Sovannarith, First Deputy Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, said that in the past, the National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) had allowed 18 banks and two microfinance institutions to provide bank services through the referral model only. This means that banking and financial institutions can refer customers to partner insurance companies without the right to sell insurance products directly.
He added that the authorization of this model only introduces the customer as an obstacle to the insurance company can not provide a wide range of banking services to customers, and this permission has not yet been clearly regulated because it is a test phase of the market.
Mr. Bou Chanphirou, Director General of the Insurance Regulator, said that the insurance sector and the banking and financial sector are two pillars that are closely related to each other in the financial sector in providing rich and comprehensive financial services to the people with the environment. .
