(Siem Reap): This morning, June 3, 2021, the Siem Reap Provincial Advisory Committee on Women and Children's Affairs held an orientation meeting on the promotion of access to care and development for children with disabilities.
The meeting was chaired by Ms. Sin Nam, Provincial Councilor and Chairperson of the Provincial Advisory Committee on Women and Children's Affairs, with the participation of the leaders of the Departments, Municipal and District Authorities, and Women's Affairs Officers. And 6 local children and representatives of civil society organizations.
The purpose of this meeting was to raise awareness of the importance of environmental education for children and support services for children with disabilities, coordination mechanisms, and support from stakeholders at the sub-national level.
Speaking at the opening of the meeting, Ms. Sin Nam stated that environmental early childhood education was organized by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports with the aim of improving access to early childhood education for children with disabilities and raising awareness. Kindergarten teachers and parents about the benefits of early childhood education for children with disabilities.
She added that after implementing a comprehensive early childhood education program over the past few years, there have been a number of challenges, such as the identification of young children with disabilities, limited awareness among parents on care and the cost of education. Of young children with disabilities Finding and providing support and development services for children with severe disabilities is limited.
According to Ms. Sin Nam, in the six target districts, there are 98 children with birth defects, 35 of whom are female. The meeting also aims to address all challenges and promote cooperation among relevant departments to contribute to the implementation of early childhood protection and development policies.
The meeting will also help orient with relevant departments and target districts in order to promote access to care and development for young children with disabilities, promote awareness of the importance of early childhood education, and support services for children with disabilities. As a mechanism for coordinating stakeholders at the sub-national level and also confirmed the expected results of the meeting.
