(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ros Sovacha, Spokesman of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, confirmed to Fresh News that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports will soon hold the first National Student Competition under the President. Learning by creating a project "Desire", the first project-based learning competition organized by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports for students from grades 7 to 12 across the country.
He said that the first nationwide student competition, the study by creating a project "desire" has the following goals:
1: Enhancing students' learning through new learning methods: collaborative learning, critical thinking, problem-solving learning, and project-based learning.
2: Support students to achieve the highest level of proficiency gained from each lesson in the national curriculum by creating a project
3: Encourage the sharing, discussion, improvement and sharing of experiences among students on the results of projects they create.
He added that the event, called "Desire", will connect a deeper understanding of the lessons of the classroom with real life in society. Students can be most actively involved in the learning process and associate learning with their interests, interests, skills and social interactions.
The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports hopes that within two or three years, if educational institutions cooperate in implementing this program and encourage students to engage in active learning in this program, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports can create a repository of The most comprehensive "student-produced digital content" for all textbook-based and grade-level lessons.
