On June 2, 2021, Phnom Penh Capital Hall issued a decision announcing a temporary suspension of activities, occupations or businesses at high risk of contracting Kovid 19 and gathering no more than 15 people from Zero from June 3 to June 16, 2021.
The decision is as follows:
Article 1: Administrative Rules are temporarily suspended for activities, occupations or businesses that are at high risk of spreading Kovid-19 disease and private gatherings or gatherings in Phnom Penh for a period of 14 (fourteen) days from zero on June 3, 2021 to June 16, 2021.
Article 2: During the issuance of administrative measures, the following activities, occupations or businesses with a high risk of spreading Kovid-19 disease are temporarily suspended as follows:
Schools, including public and private vocational training schools, except for schools that provide online training - All kinds of entertainment business, such as karaoke, bars, discos, teak, beer gardens and casinos - Resorts, museums and amusement parks - Massage business, cinema, theater Arts, gyms and sports centers.
In addition to the business activities that have been temporarily suspended as set out above, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will decide to suspend other business activities according to the actual development situation in accordance with the need to fight and prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
