(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Vandeth, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications of Cambodia, on June 2, 2021, came out to confirm some of the reasons that make the telephone and internet service in Cambodia inconvenient. At the same time, he also put out some measures immediately to solve the problem ahead.
The Cambodian Minister of Posts and Telecommunications' revelation comes after a series of complaints from residents about the disruption of Cambodia's telephone and internet services, making it difficult for them to use and criticizing Deduct his money without giving notice.
Regarding the problems of the telephone system and the internet, Mr. Chea Vandeth stated some of the reasons that he researched during his tenure as Minister for more than a year. The reasons are:
* In the past, there was only one antenna company to serve 3,000 people, but now the area has grown to 10,000 and there are more passers-by, so many users have disrupted the service. In another example, the antenna poles were so far apart that he did not plant any more.
* Borey construction factor. Some cities allow exclusive internet service providers to increase prices and provide limited service. Some Boreys do not have land for building antenna towers, making it impossible to have antenna towers in the Borey.
* Population factor. Some people are not allowed to build more antennas for fear of harming their health.
In relation to the above case, especially the problems caused by the construction of Borey, the Minister took the following measures:
1: Assign teams to all cities to measure services everywhere, and the Ministry buys millions of dollars for measuring equipment across the country.
2: The Ministry is negotiating with an APP for people to use, and when his phone is out of service, the Ministry will receive information immediately and easy to solve.
