The Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province has strongly ordered the professional officers and authorities of Kampong Leng District to immediately inspect and search for those who used the machine to steal and clear the state's flooded forest land in Plou Touk commune.
(Kampong Chhnang): 23.40 hectares of land in 3 areas in Plou Touk commune, Kampong Leng district were stolen by the villagers and some commune leaders. In this case, the competent authorities and authorities of Kampong Leng district are making a report to the provincial governor to ask for a decision.
After the media reported to the provincial governor on May 30, 2021, related to a group of crooks who used machines to clear the state's flooded forest land in the commune of Plou Touk in Kampong Leng district. Immediately, the provincial governor also ordered the district working group and professional officers to inspect and investigate the above case immediately.
Mr. Ly La, Director of Kampong Chhnang Fisheries Administration, who led the team to investigate this case, told Fresh News on the afternoon of June 2, 2021 that on May 30 and 31, 2021, professional officers and Kampong Leng district authorities cooperated to inspect and research in Plou Touk commune.
As a result, 23.40 hectares of flooded forest land in 3 areas were found in 6 locations in 3 areas in Plou Touk commune. Some states, of course. In this case, the authorities and professional officers searched and found 22 families involved, including some commune councilors, roads and boats, who used stolen machinery to clear the state's flooded forest land.
The district chief said that some of the land that was cleared last year had already been banned, but this year, some of the above opportunists continue to clear state land as additional property. This is the competent authority to build a case to send to court is not to be tolerated, because all land in the flooded forest is protected by the state, the law on fisheries strictly prohibits any person from violating.
In particular, some of the land that has been cleared this year, most people have cleared the back of their houses, more than the land allocated by the authorities from 50 meters to more than 100 meters to enjoy while the authorities distributed land Housing for them is only 20 meters by 100 meters.
Currently, the provincial authorities have submitted a request for a sub-plot of land at Veal Sra Nge, more than 1,000 hectares, from the Royal Government to distribute to the people in the commune of Plou Touk village who have moved their floating houses, he said. Come and live on land for cultivation, because the land there is already there, there is no forest. So the authorities are considering you and please wait a minute.
