According to the Dictionary of Economic Sciences of the National Council for the Khmer Language, published in 2019, "Opportunity" corresponds to the English word Opportunity, which means that the appropriate circumstance or evolution is the time, the opportunity, the favorable opportunity to take advantage of something or multiplication. Wealth is emerging, but taking advantage of it can be risky and requires a strong commitment and sufficient resources to take advantage of it.
For example, the global economic crisis of 2008-2009 provided an opportunity for Cambodia to develop its potential agricultural sector. To achieve this, Cambodia needs substantial human and financial resources to invest in its essential physical infrastructure.
Opportunity in some circumstances can be used synonymously with the word "opportunity", but generally the word "opportunity" is used to denote a simple time or circumstance. For example, today the sky is clear. Therefore, it is a good opportunity for farmers to dry their rice.
