Authorities are rehabilitating the Toul Pong II Canal and are digging to rehabilitate the Moor Canal to release water from people's villages in the southwestern part of Phnom Penh and from Drainage Station 5 to Boeung Tumpun Pumping Station.
According to Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, on June 2, following the instructions of Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh, the drainage unit of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh Has been working to restore the Toul Pong 2 canal to open the water flow quickly to release water from people's homes this rainy season.
Mr. Duong Chansarath stated that the canal is 6,100 meters long, starting from National Road 3, passing Sangkat Choam Chao I, Sangkat Choam Chao II in Por Sen Chey district and crossing to Sangkat Prey Sar, dropping to the Prek Ha bridge, which is 10 meters to 15 meters wide. By place. The site was operational on May 31 and will be completed in August 2021.
Separately, the Moor Canal, located in Moor Village, Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor, is more than 3 kilometers long from the 5th Drainage Pumping Station to the Boeung Tumpun Pumping Station in Sangkat Boeung Tumpun II, Khan Meanchey. Villages were flooded by the rainy season.
Mr. Mao Bunthoeun, Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Phnom Penh, said this morning, June 2, that under the guidance of Mr. Khuong Sreng, the team of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Phnom Penh has been working to restore the canal. On February 18, 2021 and scheduled to be completed by the end of August 2021, with a length of more than 3 kilometers from 20 meters to 30 meters from the pumping station 5 to the pumping station.
