In late April, Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen issued an order to vaccinate people in the former Red Zone from the age of 18 to vaccinate 19 to develop immunity and to protect people from the 19-year-old disease. It was exploding in the former Red Zone.
Due to the former Red Zone being a complex area and a high risk area for 19 Kovid infections, Samdech Techo Hun Sen assigned the task of vaccinating the former Red Zone to the military. After receiving this order, the army medical team started the vaccination operation on May 1, 2021.
Vaccination in the former Red Zone was initially planned in only four districts, including Meanchey, Por Senchey, Dangkor and Kambol, with a population of just over 500,000. But then the vaccination area was expanded to six districts, adding Russey Keo and Toul Kork districts, and the number of vaccinated people increased from more than 500,000 to more than 1 million.
Vaccination operations in the former Red Zone Initially, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, was scheduled to complete one month to complete both the first and second doses. But now the operation is not over yet because the location and the number of people to be injected have increased.
However, General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Operation Kovid 19 Vaccination, the Ministry of National Defense considers this operation to be a great success and historic because of the time the army vaccinated the people. Nearly 1 million people.
General Ith Sarath said that this success was achieved due to the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the constant monitoring of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense.
This success would not have been possible without the dedication and determination of the army, the vaccination team from all units, the close cooperation of local authorities and the media.
General Ith Sarath praised the perseverance and perseverance of his comrades in the vaccination mission in the Red Zone. Mr. Ith Sarath also thanked for the dedication and responsible spirit of the task and hoped that all fighters will continue to adhere to this spirit to achieve other missions submitted by the Royal Government.
According to General Ith Sarath, the first vaccination in the former Red Zone in the six districts is scheduled to close this week.
The public has expressed admiration and admiration for the Ministry of Defense's vaccination team, who have worked tirelessly to vaccinate people in the former Red Zone despite facing the 19-year-old Kovid infection and are exhausted. Anyway, that. In particular, the team vaccinated at a fast pace.
Residents of the former Red Zone have all expressed their happiness after receiving the vaccine. They thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for considering and giving them priority in getting the vaccine. They also thanked the army for always carrying out front-line operations to alleviate difficulties.
