(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has published its 2020 Financial Stability Report, which presents recent developments in the macroeconomic and financial sectors and challenges.
This 2020 Financial Stability Report discusses the prospects and risks that the financial sector will face during the uncertainties of the local, regional and global economy due to the outbreak of Kovid 19. .
This booklet will be used as a reference for individuals working in the financial sector, intellectuals, development partners and stakeholders to better understand the financial stability situation in Cambodia.
Please be informed that 2020 is a challenging year with the spread of Kovid 19 disease affecting the world economy and financial markets. Like other countries, Cambodia has been hit hard by the spread of Kovid 19, which has had a negative economic growth after achieving an average growth rate of around 8% over the past two decades.
Despite the impact of the Kovid 19 outbreak, the banking sector in Cambodia remains resilient due to the introduction of proactive and effective macro- and micro-precautionary measures.
In this uncertain situation, the National Bank of Cambodia continues to monitor the latest developments and is ready to take the necessary measures to continue to contribute to supporting economic activities in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government. Prey Veng finds 65 more Kovid positives in 6 districts
