According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's personal assistant, after the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the US Deputy Secretary of State to consider and resolve the debt owed by Cambodia to the United States during the Lon Nol regime of nearly 700 million. Dollars (both original and original).
Mr. Eang Sophalleth stated that Samdech Techo proposed three mechanisms for resolving this debt, including: 1: allowing Cambodia to repay the debt gradually, 2: repayment through the interest rate repayment program at one percent and third: debt repayment. More than 70 percent of Cambodia's development assistance is in the areas of education, culture and demining, as well as unexploded ordnance.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth further stated that in response to this request, the US Deputy Secretary of State promised to take the request to Mr. Joe Biden for review and resolution.
The Republican government of General Lon Nol owed the United States government about $ 274 million, which has now risen to nearly $ 700 million. Most of the Republican debt at the time was used for military service and warfare.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen used to consider this debt as a dirty debt, like taking the burden on the heads of the Cambodian people, because the budget to serve the military sector at that time led to the flames of war and caused great suffering for the Cambodian people.
Please be informed that in the current meeting with Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the US Deputy Secretary of State expressed great satisfaction with the cooperation with Cambodia in many areas, such as the discovery of US military remains in Cambodia, cooperation in combat. Terrorism, humanitarian activities such as docking the Western Dam.
The Deputy Foreign Minister also mentioned opportunities to expand cooperation in the oil and gas sector, investment in water, infrastructure, green energy and other issues.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen agreed with what the Deputy Foreign Minister said. He also thanked the United States for helping to bring peace to Cambodia and for providing both direct and indirect development assistance.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also congratulated the United States on its excellent results in the fight against Kovid 19.
