The following is a press release from the Koh Kong Provincial Administration: Chinese President Xi Jinping has always cared about the future of children
BEIJING: Chinese President Xi Jinping has always cared about the future of children. He always congratulates children all over China on the occasion of International Children's Day on June 1. He often went to meet children and youth to show greetings and care, and Chinese children are affectionately called "Mr. Ta Xi".
Xi Jinping was born into a revolutionary family, strict home education, his childhood was very simple. In an interview with China Central Television in 2003, he recalled that at that time, the clothes we usually wore had a lot of patches and had to be worn by our brothers and sisters.
Xi Jinping has six siblings, so when he was young he usually had to wear his sister's clothes. "I absolutely do not want to wear clothes and shoes with flowers, but I have to," he said.
In the minds of Chinese children, Xi Jinping is a well-known figure and a close and loving grandfather. On May 21, 2013, Xi Jinping visited the earthquake victims in Lushan City, Sichuan Province.
