South Korean Administration Provides 19 Kovid 19 Diagnostic Equipment to the Royal Government of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Government and people of South Korea provide a package of 19 kovid diagnostic kits worth a total of approximately US $ 300,000 to the Royal Government of Cambodia to contribute to the fight against Kovid 19 in Cambodia.
The handover ceremony of this medical device was held on Tuesday afternoon, June 1, 2021. The South Korean side was represented by Mr. Park Heung-kang, Ambassador of the Republic of Korea to Cambodia, and the Cambodian side was represented by Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health.
During the ceremony, the Ambassador commended the Government of Cambodia for its relentless efforts to respond to the spread of Kovid 19 with the introduction of measures to reduce the spread of the disease. In particular, efforts to vaccinate 19 people against measles have reached more than 2.5 million people.
The ambassador also stressed that since the outbreak of Kovid 19 in Cambodia, Korea has not hesitated to cooperate with Cambodia to fight the virus.
On that occasion, the Ambassador expressed high confidence that Cambodia will be successful in overcoming the Kovid 19 epidemic, and the Korean government will continue to work closely with Cambodia to strengthen good relations and cooperation between the two countries.
Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said on that occasion that the traditional Cambodian-Korean friendship has been continuously strengthened and expanded and provided many grants to contribute to the improvement of the Cambodian health sector. Especially since the outbreak of Kovid-19, Korea has provided some medical equipment and funding.
The Minister said that the humanitarian assistance of the Korean side today will contribute to preventing the spread of Kovid-19 in Cambodia.
The Minister thanked the Korean government and people, especially the Korean Ambassador to Cambodia, for facilitating the smooth delivery process. He strongly hopes that the Republic of Korea will continue to provide assistance.
