(Phnom Penh): Operation of vaccination against Kovid 19 to the people in the red area in Phnom Penh under the direct command of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia is continuing in the first and second doses under high attention. From the Vaccination Team of the Ministry of National Defense to ensure that all citizens are vaccinated against Kovid 19.
In the past 29 days, the Ministry of Defense vaccination team has given the first dose to more than 870,000 people, while the second dose, which started on May 16, has given more than 610,000 people.
The red areas where the army is vaccinating include Khan Meanchey, Khan Dangkor, Khan Kambol, Khan Por Senchey, Khan Russey Keo and Khan Toul Kork.
General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Vaccination Team in the Red Zone, noted that the vaccination process in both the first and second doses was going well under close supervision. High from the team.
Although the team is working on the second dose, the first dose is still ongoing. On May 29, the first dose was given to 20,361 people.
With this vaccination process, the General continued to remind all vaccination teams to carefully examine the vaccination of the people to make sure that the interval between the first dose to the second dose is 14 days. And technically correct injections to ensure that people are vaccinated against Kovid 19.
General Ith Sarath also confirmed and called on people who go to the second dose to take the documents and meet some important conditions.
Documents and conditions that must be followed for this second dose include: Bring the first dose form, where the first dose should be given, the second dose should be given in the same place, know the timing of the injection. Second (every 14 days) to avoid accumulation and affect the effectiveness of the drug. In particular, people with Kovid 19 are not allowed to take the second dose.
Mr. Ith Sarath also called on people who have already been vaccinated with the second dose to keep the temporary immunization form properly, not to lose or tear it in exchange for the immunization card that the team is producing. In particular, those who have received a vaccination card must also be careful not to lose because it may be necessary to use in the future.
At the same time, General Ith Sarath also called on the people in the red area who have not been vaccinated the first dose to participate in the vaccination, because the team continues to give the first dose, and please participate in the implementation of the rules. Health when going to get vaccinated.
General Ith Sarath has already called on the first and last vaccinators to come and give the second dose at their own time so that the vaccine can be more effective in combating Kovid 19. The call comes after he finds that it is time for some second dose to be missed.
The people who received the first and second doses were happy and thanked Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen for seeking the vaccine and giving priority to the red zone.
Residents also thanked the vaccination team for paying close attention to their vaccination work.
Despite the two doses of vaccination, General Ith Sarath reminded the people to continue to follow the rules of the Ministry of Health, especially the recommendation of Samdech Techo "3 do not 3 protect" to ensure that Kovid 19 is not infected. . Minister Chea Vandeth Receives and Discusses with Singaporean Ambassador to Cambodia
