General knowledge: How did people in the Stone Age live?
(World): As we all know, in the Stone Age 2.6 million years ago, the life of the first people was very simple, but by the Middle Ages, they began to create tools and can move. Places to go to places in Africa, Europe and Asia. How did people in those Stone Age live like that?
In addition to creating tools, they also know how to hunt wild animals, both small and large. These people have created different living societies depending on the area in which they live.
In addition, they also know how to develop their society into a personal tradition and continue to develop that tradition further through the development of language, beliefs, religions and arts.
Some anthropologists believe that the first humans lived in small, isolated groups. In their living, whenever the weather is bad, they move to live in caves or caves if there is one in that area. As for food and water, whenever there is a decrease and it is difficult to find, all the people will move to another area.
Women and children, on the other hand, are responsible for finding natural harvests such as fruits, grains, tubers, eggs, birds, and other edible things. Generally, women and children do not walk far from where they live, the reason is to make it easier to care for their children.
