Samdech Techo Hun Sen: In June, another 4.5 million doses of vaccine will arrive, making Cambodia have enough vaccines to give to the people as planned (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, emphasized that the vaccine against Another 4.5 million doses of Kovid 19 will arrive in Cambodia this June. Samdech Techo also stated that the plan to vaccinate 10 million people can be achieved by the end of 2021 or the beginning of 2022.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's confirmation was made through a special voice message on the Kovid 19 vaccination plan this Saturday, May 29, 2021.
In this audio message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia will have enough Kovid 19 vaccine to be given to the people just before and after. Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked the people to understand and wait for the vaccination according to the plan prepared by the Royal Government.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also highlighted that Cambodia will complete the vaccination of 10 million people this year or at the latest by early 2022.
"We will have enough vaccines to vaccinate," Hun Sen said. About 4.5 million more doses are planned for June and beyond. We will be able to inject at least 5 million to 6 million before the end of this year out of 10 million. "And we will strive to achieve 10 million vaccinations this year, or at the latest by early next year, so that all of our people can be vaccinated."
However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called on people who have not been vaccinated to continue to adhere to the rules of protection against Kovid 19, using the "3 prevent and 3 do not" and for those who have already been vaccinated. Do not abandon this rule either.
