Kovid-19 outbreak in Vietnam threatens global technology supply chain
HANOI: The rapid spread of Kovid 19 has caused production declines in factories in Vietnam's northern industrial provinces, according to industry sources. This is according to the release by Reuters on Friday, May 28, 2021.
After successfully controlling the Kovid 19 epidemic in 2020, Vietnam is now facing an unprecedented community outbreak. More than 3,000 people in 63 cities and provinces have been reported infected since the end of April.
The capital, Hanoi, and the southern business district of Ho Chi Minh City have closed restaurants and banned public gatherings to fight Kovid 19.
Sources from four large companies said their operations were affected as some areas were closed, while others were required to shift shifts to reduce the risk of copying 19. This raises concerns about disruption of the supply chain.
