NEC Holds Online Consultation Meeting on 2021 Commune / Sangkat Council Election Pilot Election
(Phnom Penh): The National Election Committee (NEC) this morning, May 28, 2021, held a consultative meeting on the 2021 Commune / Sangkat Council Election. First online in the context of Kovid 19 with all stakeholders.
The meeting was chaired by Mr. Dim Sovannarom, Member and Spokesperson of the NEC, and Mr. Sik Bun Hok, Chairman of the National Election Committee.
The 2021 Commune / Sangkat Council Election will be held on Sunday, June 20, 2021. The purpose of this pilot election is to evaluate the effectiveness of modernizing the current electoral process in the run-up to future elections. This was highlighted by Mr. Dim Sovannarom in the online consultation meeting on the 2021 Commune / Sangkat Council Election.
He said that the NEC held a pilot election for the purpose of monitoring, verifying and evaluating the effectiveness of modernizing the election process, such as:
* Use of political party registration software and online voter list * Use of ballpoint pens * Use of online election verification and summarying software Covered
Covers the main processes on Election Day through the following systematic programs:
* Program to receive, summarize, send and announce the preliminary results of the election * Program to verify and summarize the provisional results of the election * Program to verify and summarize the official results of the election * Program to allocate seats and list the names of elected candidates .
