Asia Vision Institute to Organize Training Program for Journalists on "Geopolitical Analysis and Foreign Policy"
(Phnom Penh): The Asian Institute of Vision (AVI) will organize a training program for journalists on "Geopolitical Analysis and Foreign Policy". The opening ceremony will be held on Monday, May 31, 2021.
Well-known experts in geopolitical and foreign policy analysis will be invited to train in this program. This training course will be held every Tuesday via Video Zoom from June 1 to August 3, 2021. Each session lasts 1 hour and 30 minutes, requiring participants to study a total of 20 sessions over a period of 10 weeks.
The purpose of this training is to (1) provide Cambodian journalists with the necessary knowledge related to geography, politics and foreign policy at the national, regional and international levels, and (2) build the capacity of Cambodian journalists to be able to provide honest and balanced information. And (3) allow journalists to build relationships with other actors from government, the private sector, and civil society.
