(Phnom Penh): Thirty-five containers of frozen goods and meat imported from India and arrived in Cambodia before the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia decided to temporarily suspend imports were allowed to circulate in the Cambodian market after a positive Kovid test. 19.
The decision to allow the above 35 containers of frozen goods and frozen meat imported from India was made at the request of the Commission for the Prevention of the Extinction of Kovid 19 after a negative Kovid-19 test on those goods and frozen meat. .
Mr. Phan Oun, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Consumer Protection, Competition and Anti-Fraud (CPC) of the Ministry of Commerce, confirmed that these goods and frozen meat are all goods. Arrived before the Royal Government decided to suspend imports.
Mr. Phan Oun added that after testing 35 containers of frozen goods and frozen meat imported from India, no positive Kovid-19 was found, the commission also asked Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, Minister of Economy and Finance, to Do the export.
At the same time, Mr. Phan Oun also stated that the Royal Government continues to temporarily suspend the import and suspension of customs clearance for frozen meat and frozen goods from India without import. That no.
On May 1, 2021, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia decided to temporarily suspend the importation and suspension of customs clearance for frozen meat and other potentially frozen items. India.
According to a letter sent to the head of the branch department and the Office of Customs and Excise, which was received by Fresh News, the decision was made in response to the severe situation of the 199 Kovid epidemic in India and in accordance with Guidance of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia has temporarily recommended the import of frozen meat and other high-risk frozen goods originating from India as follows:
* Suspend the import of these goods, suspend the customs clearance for those goods that have already arrived at the customs clearance or inventory.
* Cooperate with the Commission on the research and testing of various viruses, especially Kovid 19 virus, and participate in the implementation of the Commission's measures or decisions on matters related to those products.
