"Mother's Craft" project, China's poverty alleviation plan will enter Cambodia
BEIJING: The "Mother's Craft" project is a poverty alleviation project that Chinese companies have achieved in the Yi Langshan Autonomous Region of Sichuan Province. By hand-designing and processing second-hand clothes and reselling them to lift poor women out of poverty and into a more prosperous life, as well as promote the development of intangible cultural heritage and traditional handicrafts.
This sustainable public interest project will go into Cambodia. Chinese companies, through the Lancang-Mekong Cooperation Mechanism and other Sino-Cambodian cooperation projects, promote the exchange of friendly relations between the Chinese and Cambodian peoples through practical implementation and promote the development of international poverty alleviation work.
The "Mother Crafts" project seeks out women in poor areas who specialize in handicrafts through technical and production training, collaborating with designers and product designers by a team of professionals who bring products to China. The product will focus on young Chinese groups and focus on integrating the trends that young people love.
