Some people do not see the second dose! General Ith Sarath calls for second dose for effective anti-Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Vaccination Task Force in the Red Zone, urges people in the Red Zone who have already received the first dose to get vaccinated. The second dose (14 days after the first dose) to be immunized and effective against Kovid 19.
General Ith Sarath's call came after a review of vaccination data showed that a small number of people could not be vaccinated as the deadline had arrived.
"I urge all our brothers and sisters to come and get the second dose so that we can be more resistant and more effective in preventing and combating Kovid 19 virus." If we do not give a second dose, the vaccine will not be as effective in fighting Kovid 19. So please come and get the second dose of vaccine for everyone at the place where we give the first dose. This is the appeal of General Ith Sarath.
In connection with the vaccination, General Ith Sarath also called on the people who received the second dose of the vaccine to ask for a vaccination card from the vaccination team and take good care not to lose it.
During a visit to the vaccination site, General Ith Sarath observed that some people who had already received the second dose did not seem to be busy getting vaccination cards. General Ith Sarath thinks that maybe the people do not understand the value of the vaccine.
General Ith Sarath said the vaccine was very valuable for future use. "Vaccination cards are proof that we have been vaccinated, that vaccines can be used for work and other necessities," he said. In addition, this card can also be used for entry into any country in the future.
"This vaccination card is very important for us to use in our daily lives in the future," said Ith Sarath. I see some of our brothers, he is not busy taking cards at all. "Therefore, I would like to appeal to the people who received the second dose of vaccination to find a vaccination card and take good care of it so that it does not get lost."
