ASEAN-US Foreign Ministers' Special Meeting Postponed
(Phnom Penh): The ASEAN-US Foreign Ministers' Special Meeting, scheduled for this week's video, has been postponed indefinitely. This is according to Mr. Koy Kuong, spokesman for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia.
The spokesman did not elaborate on the reason for the postponement, but said it was "impossible" due to technical issues. Koy Kuong also did not know the new date for the meeting.
"Please be informed that the outcome of the ASEAN-US Foreign Ministers' Special Meeting is not as planned, as this meeting has been postponed due to technical issues," he said. "
According to a press release from the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the ASEAN-US Foreign Ministers' Special Meeting is scheduled to be videotaped on May 25, 2021. Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, is also expected to attend the meeting.
The actions of this world power are seen as despising ASEAN.
The ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting with Anthony Blinken is expected to discuss ways to further enhance cooperation and partnership between ASEAN and the United States, especially in addressing the current global welfare crisis. And exchange views on regional and international issues of common interest.
The video meeting also reflects the political will and commitment to promote the ASEAN-US Strategic Partnership for long-term cooperation for peace, stability, security and socio-economic development inside and outside the region.
