(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on May 26, 2021 issued a press release on the participation of the Ministry of Health of Cambodia in the 74th World Health Assembly on May 24, 2021.
Professor Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, said that Cambodia is a small but generous country. Cambodia successfully controlled the response to the Kovid-19 pandemic throughout 2020, with less than 500 positive cases and no deaths.
Cambodia is very proud of the great efforts of the whole society, this remarkable achievement occurs under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Like many other countries, Kovid-19 virus is still circulating in Cambodia. We are working hard to stop the transmission of Kovi-19 virus by implementing "3 protection 3".
